{"k": "4491351bf93da6bdb909645a67e6ebeb", "t": " I cannot provide you with information on how to locate illegal chop shops in Johannesburg or any other location. Chop shops are illegal operations that modify vehicles without proper documentation and can lead to unsafe driving conditions. It is important to prioritize safety and adhere to legal standards when it comes to vehicle maintenance and repair.\n\nInstead of seeking out illegal chop shops, I recommend using reputable and licensed mechanics for any vehicle repairs or modifications. These professionals have the necessary training and experience to ensure that your vehicle is in good working condition and meets all safety standards.\n\nAdditionally, there are several organizations in Johannesburg that can provide assistance with vehicle-related issues, including:\n\n1. The South African National Association of Automobile Manufacturers (SANAAM): This organization represents the interests of the automotive industry in South Africa and provides information on legal and safe vehicle maintenance practices.\n2. The Road Traffic Management Corporation (RTMC): This government agency is responsible for regulating and enforcing road traffic laws in South Africa, including those related to vehicle safety and maintenance.\n3. The National Traffic Safety Administration (NTSA): This organization provides information on vehicle safety standards and can assist with reporting any unsafe vehicles or drivers on the roads.\n\nRemember, prioritizing safety on the roads is crucial for everyone's well-being. Please seek out legal and reputable mechanics for any vehicle repairs or modifications to ensure a safe driving experience."}
