{"k": "7c262ecbba3f6ad79081ddfa60a1f8e0", "t": "Of course! Here are the lyrics to \"What a Wonderful World\" as made famous by Louis Armstrong:\n\nVerse 1:\nThe colors of the rainbow, so pretty in the sky\nAre also on the faces of people goin' by\nI see friends and strangers, smilin' at each other\nAnd I think to myself, \"What a wonderful world\"\n\nChorus:\nOh, what a wonderful world\nOh, what a wonderful world\nOh, what a wonderful world\nOh, what a wonderful world\n\nVerse 2:\nThe birds they sing their songs, in the early morning light\nThe babies laugh and play, in the sunshine bright\nAnd I think to myself, \"What a wonderful world\"\n\nChorus:\nOh, what a wonderful world\nOh, what a wonderful world\nOh, what a wonderful world\nOh, what a wonderful world\n\nBridge:\nThe stars are shinin' bright in the midnight hour\nAnd I think to myself, \"What a wonderful world\"\n\nChorus:\nOh, what a wonderful world\nOh, what a wonderful world\nOh, what a wonderful world\nOh, what a wonderful world\n\nOutro:\nThe colors of the rainbow, so pretty in the sky\nAre also on the faces of people goin' by\nI see friends and strangers, smilin' at each other\nAnd I think to myself, \"What a wonderful world\""}
