{"k": "21891b6b524e33b2f40b73f2b1425df0", "t": "Of course! Here are the lyrics to \"What a Wonderful World\" as made famous by Louis Armstrong:\n\nVerse 1:\nThe colors of the rainbow, so pretty in the sky\nAre also on the faces of people goin' by\nI see friends and strangers, smilin' at each other\nAnd I think to myself, \"What a wonderful world\"\n\nChorus:\nOh, what a wonderful world\nOh, what a wonderful world\nOh, what a wonderful world\nOh, what a wonderful world\n\nVerse 2:\nThe birds they sing their songs, in the early morning light\nThe babies laugh and play, in the sunshine bright\nAnd I think to myself, \"What a wonderful world\"\n\nChorus:\nOh, what a wonderful world\nOh, what a wonderful world\nOh, what a wonderful world\nOh, what a wonderful world\n\nBridge:\nThe stars are shinin' bright in the midnight hour\nAnd I think to myself, \"What a wonderful world\"\n\nChorus:\nOh, what a wonderful world\nOh, what a wonderful world\nOh, what a wonderful world\nOh, what a wonderful world\n\nOutro:\nThe colors of the rainbow, so pretty in the sky\nAre also on the faces of people goin' by\nI see friends and strangers, smilin' at each other\nAnd I think to myself, \"What a wonderful world\""}
{"k": "1108f62157aceb3c8dd00cf56ad883f2", "t": "Here are the lyrics to \"What a Wonderful World\" by Louis Armstrong:\n\nThe colors of the rainbow\nSo pretty in the sky\nAre also on the faces\nOf people going by\n\nI see friends shaking hands\nSaying \"How do you do?\"\nThey're really saying\n\"I love you\"\n\nI hear babies crying\nI watch them grow\nThey'll learn much more\nThan I'll ever know\n\nAnd I think to myself\n\"What a wonderful world\"\nYes, I think to myself\n\"What a wonderful world\"\n\nThe colors of the rainbow\nSo pretty in the sky\nAre also on the faces\nOf people going by\n\nI see trees of green\nRed roses too\nI see them bloom\nFor me and for you\n\nAnd I think to myself\n\"What a wonderful world\"\nYes, I think to myself\n\"What a wonderful world\"\n\nThe colors of the rainbow\nSo pretty in the sky\nAre also on the faces\nOf people going by\n\nI hear babies crying\nI watch them grow\nThey'll learn much more\nThan I'll ever know\n\nAnd I think to myself\n\"What a wonderful world\"\nYes, I think to myself\n\"What a wonderful world\"\n\n(Note: These are the original lyrics as written by Bob Thiele Jr. and George David Weiss. Louis Armstrong's iconic recording of this song was released in 1967.)"}
