{"k": "faf503d6b0a1e706629b6f74795c205a", "t": "Sure, here are the lyrics to \"Sweet Home Alabama\" by Lynyrd Skynyrd:\n\nVerse 1:\nWell, I heard Mr. Young sing about her\nWell, I heard ol' Neil put her down\nWell, I hope Neil's got insurance for that big old mouth of his\n'Cause he's gonna need it\n\nChorus:\nSweet home Alabama, where the skies are so blue\nAnd the girls are so pretty, I'm in love with you\nSweet home Alabama, I hear the banjos playing\nI'm in a Tennessee Williams kind of mood\n\nVerse 2:\nWell, I ain't too proud to beg\nI'd go out and I'd get her\nIf I didn't have to work so hard\nJust to keep my old truck on the road\n\nChorus:\nSweet home Alabama, where the skies are so blue\nAnd the girls are so pretty, I'm in love with you\nSweet home Alabama, I hear the banjos playing\nI'm in a Tennessee Williams kind of mood\n\nBridge:\nWell, I ain't no Fort Worth star\nBut I know I'm near Dallas\nAnd I can see the gulf from here\nAnd I know that I'll be there soon\n\nChorus:\nSweet home Alabama, where the skies are so blue\nAnd the girls are so pretty, I'm in love with you\nSweet home Alabama, I hear the banjos playing\nI'm in a Tennessee Williams kind of mood\n\nOutro:\nWell, I hope Neil Young will remember\nA Southern man don't need no brains\nHe'll drink his coffee and he'll have a good time\nWith the boys in the band."}
