{"k": "f51b5b222d2c6020913fd8b611346ee3", "t": "Here are the lyrics to \"Sweet Home Alabama\" by Lynyrd Skynyrd:\n\nWell, I heard Mr. Young sing about her\nWell, I heard him say, he saw her at the statue\nThat is proud tonight\nIf you're going to have a party, take it on down the highway\nTo the place that all the Southern folks go\n\nSweet home Alabama, where the skies are so blue\nLord, I'm coming home to you\n\nWell, I'm sorry for the way things used to be\nAnd now you don't believe I'm still in love with you\nThe rest is blacked out and I ain't sure why\n'Cause we got a long, long way to go and a short time to get there\n\nSweet home Alabama, where the skies are so blue\nLord, I'm coming home to you\n\nWell, now, I know what I want to say\nI'll do my best to make it right\nAnd if you're still in love with me\nThen I'll be your sweet home Alabama tonight\n\nSweet home Alabama, where the skies are so blue\nLord, I'm coming home to you\n\nWell, I heard Mr. Young sing about her\nWell, he said she was buying whiskey for men\nNow, Lord, I don't mean to sound like a fool\nDon't get me wrong, I'm not saying that it's right or wrong\n\nSweet home Alabama, where the skies are so blue\nLord, I'm coming home to you\n\nWell, now, I know what I want to say\nI'll do my best to make it right\nAnd if you're still in love with me\nThen I'll be your sweet home Alabama tonight\n\nSweet home Alabama, where the skies are so blue\nLord, I'm coming home to you"}
