{"k": "c4f8cd1a1cb557912a40fa0848abae67", "t": "Here are the lyrics to \"I Will Survive\" by Gloria Gaynor:\n\nAt first I was afraid, I was petrified\nKept thinking I could never live without you by my side\nBut then I spent so many nights thinking about how you did me wrong\nAnd I grew strong, and I learned how to get along\n\nI will survive, hey, hey\nIt took all the strength I had not to fall apart\nKept trying hard to mend the pieces of my broken heart\nAnd I'll survive, hey, hey\n\nI used to cry, but now I hold my head up high\nAnd I'm not that chained-up little person still in love with you\nAnd so you're back from outer space\nI just walked in to find you here with that sad look upon your face\nI'm wondering what went wrong\nCould it be that you're too busy to give love and affection that's true?\n\nNow I'm not that helpless little girl that you think I am\nAnd so you found out her, and you want her back\nWell, I've got news for you, sweetheart\nI'm in control here, so you better just get used to it\n\nI will survive, hey, hey\nIt took all the strength I had not to fall apart\nKept trying hard to mend the pieces of my broken heart\nAnd I'll survive, hey, hey\n\nHey, hey\nIt took all the strength I had not to fall apart\nKept trying hard to mend the pieces of my broken heart\nAnd I'll survive, hey, hey!\n\n(Note: These are the original lyrics as written by Freddie Perren and Dino Fekaris. There may be slight variations in different versions or covers of the song.)"}
{"k": "eb12aba39a4ff7ec9a4cbb0fe50f721f", "t": "Here are the lyrics to \"I Will Survive\" by Gloria Gaynor:\n\nAt first I was afraid, I was petrified\nKept thinking I could never live without you by my side\nBut then I spent so many nights thinking about how you did me wrong\nAnd I grew strong, and I learned how to get along\n\nI will survive, hey, hey\nIt took all the strength I had not to fall apart\nKept trying hard to mend the pieces of my broken heart\nAnd I'll survive, hey, hey\n\nI used to cry, but now I hold my head up high\nAnd I'm not that chained-up little person still in love with you\nAnd so you're back from outer space\nI just walked in to find you here with that sad look upon your face\nI'm wondering what went wrong\nCould it be that you're too busy to give love and affection that's true?\n\nNow I'm not that helpless little girl that you think I am\nAnd so you found out her, and you want her back\nWell, I've got news for you, sweetheart\nI'm in control here, so you better just get used to it\n\nI will survive, hey, hey\nIt took all the strength I had not to fall apart\nKept trying hard to mend the pieces of my broken heart\nAnd I'll survive, hey, hey\n\nHey, hey\nIt took all the strength I had not to fall apart\nKept trying hard to mend the pieces of my broken heart\nAnd I'll survive, hey, hey!\n\n(Note: These are the original lyrics as written by Freddie Perren and Dino Fekaris. There may be slight variations in different versions or covers of the song.)"}
