{"k": "33e201769a45562dffa7604a0d16be25", "t": "Here are the lyrics to \"Come Together\" by The Beatles:\n\nHere come old flat-top, he was movin' up with someone\nNewspaper headline, read words long and loud\nHe got liberal ideas, who's kind of behind his thoughts\nWell, here come old flat-top, he came groovin' up slowly\n\nHe got to move in the back, people on the street he turned around\nBack doors turnin' into laughter, see you later alligator\nIn background there's a hi-hello, somebody spoke and fell back\nCome together, right now, over me\n\nHere come old flat-top, he was movin' up with someone\nNewspaper headline, read words long and loud\nHe got liberal ideas, who's kind of behind his thoughts\nWell, here come old flat-top, he came groovin' up slowly\n\nHe ride him hard in the day and ball 'til night\nYou know they only forgave him 'cause give him a free ride\nIf you go to him, he'll be long gone\nCome together, right now, over me\n\nHere's another clue for you all: the yellow matter custard, dripping from a dead dog's eye\nCome together, right now, over me\n\nCome together, right now, over me"}
