{"k": "5b2d8cb5e9fe1a4c899d4a3f31a1aca5", "t": "A classic! Here are the lyrics to \"Pinball Wizard\" by The Who:\n\nVerse 1:\nThe kids were singing, \"Pinball wizard!\"\nAs he bent and twisted, he did not know\nWhat he'd do, it was a game of skill\nIn pinball heaven, he'd be in his prime\n\nChorus:\nPinball wizard! Pinball wizard!\nHe's the king of the game!\n\nVerse 2:\nThe kids were singing, \"Pinball wizard!\"\nAs he bent and twisted, he did not know\nWhat he'd do, it was a game of skill\nIn pinball heaven, he'd be in his prime\n\nChorus:\nPinball wizard! Pinball wizard!\nHe's the king of the game!\n\nVerse 3:\nThe kids were singing, \"Pinball wizard!\"\nAs he bent and twisted, he did not know\nWhat he'd do, it was a game of skill\nIn pinball heaven, he'd be in his prime\n\nChorus:\nPinball wizard! Pinball wizard!\nHe's the king of the game!\n\nBridge:\nThe kids were singing, \"Pinball wizard!\"\nAs he bent and twisted, he did not know\nWhat he'd do, it was a game of skill\nIn pinball heaven, he'd be in his prime\n\nChorus:\nPinball wizard! Pinball wizard!\nHe's the king of the game!\n\nOutro:\nThe kids were singing, \"Pinball wizard!\"\nAs he bent and twisted, he did not know\nWhat he'd do, it was a game of skill\nIn pinball heaven, he'd be in his prime\n\nNote: These are the original lyrics as they appear on The Who's 1969 album \"Tommy\"."}
{"k": "ff198b6562e814cda634bcf9e6200710", "t": "A classic! Here are the lyrics to \"Pinball Wizard\" by The Who:\n\nVerse 1:\nThe kids were singing, \"Pinball wizard!\"\nAs he bent and twisted, he did not know\nWhat he'd do, but he knew what he'd be\nHe'd be a pinball wizard, yes indeed!\n\nChorus:\nPinball wizard! Pinball wizard!\nHe's the king of the game!\nPinball wizard! Pinball wizard!\nHe's the one they all proclaim!\n\nVerse 2:\nThe kids were singing, \"Pinball wizard!\"\nAs he bent and twisted, he did not know\nWhat he'd do, but he knew what he'd be\nHe'd be a pinball wizard, yes indeed!\n\nChorus:\nPinball wizard! Pinball wizard!\nHe's the king of the game!\nPinball wizard! Pinball wizard!\nHe's the one they all proclaim!\n\nBridge:\nThe kids were singing, \"Pinball wizard!\"\nAs he bent and twisted, he did not know\nWhat he'd do, but he knew what he'd be\nHe'd be a pinball wizard, yes indeed!\n\nChorus:\nPinball wizard! Pinball wizard!\nHe's the king of the game!\nPinball wizard! Pinball wizard!\nHe's the one they all proclaim!\n\nOutro:\nThe kids were singing, \"Pinball wizard!\"\nAs he bent and twisted, he did not know\nWhat he'd do, but he knew what he'd be\nHe'd be a pinball wizard, yes indeed!\n\nThese lyrics are from the 1969 rock opera album \"Tommy\" by The Who."}
