{"k": "19c89c711ddad3910141ab3a11907693", "t": "\nVerse 1:\nIn the town of Liverpool there's a girl I know\nWell-known for her beauty, she's got the whole town in tow\nHer name is Maggie May, and she's lighting up the night\nWith a smile so bright, it's like the sun in flight\n\nChorus:\nOh, Maggie May, you're the flower of Scotland\nAnd I'm the lucky one who gets to love you\nIn the town of Liverpool, where the wind never stops\nI'll be loving you till the end of time, my dear\n\nVerse 2:\nShe's got a way of walking that drives me wild\nAnd when she talks, her voice is like a gentle stream\nHer laughter's sweet and her eyes are bright and wide\nOh, Maggie May, I'm so glad you're by my side\n\nChorus:\nOh, Maggie May, you're the flower of Scotland\nAnd I'm the lucky one who gets to love you\nIn the town of Liverpool, where the wind never stops\nI'll be loving you till the end of time, my dear\n\nBridge:\nWe'll take a walk along the river and we'll watch the sun go down\nAnd I'll tell you all about my life in Scotland, Maggie May\nYou're the one who makes me feel so alive\nOh, Maggie May, I'm so glad you're mine\n\nChorus:\nOh, Maggie May, you're the flower of Scotland\nAnd I'm the lucky one who gets to love you\nIn the town of Liverpool, where the wind never stops\nI'll be loving you till the end of time, my dear"}
