{"k": "771d218f5838fd575ff48e386b75685c", "t": "Here are the lyrics to \"Maggie May\" by Rod Stewart:\n\nWell, she came and stood in my garden,\nWith flowers in her hair.\nJust a runaway, but I knew right then\nThat I would love her till the day I die.\n\nNow, Maggie May has got it bad,\nThink she's lost her grip on reality.\nShe's gone to the doctor, and what did he say?\n\"Leave your worries behind, dear, you're 17.\"\n\nWell, she won't find it difficult to see\nThat I'm just a poor boy, and I want to be free.\nTo look out for number one,\nIs not only natural but I hope is right.\n\nNow, Maggie May has got it bad,\nThink she's lost her grip on reality.\nShe's gone to the doctor, and what did he say?\n\"Leave your worries behind, dear, you're 17.\"\n\nWell, we'll have a good time,\nAnd we'll have a good time,\nAnd we'll have a good time,\nAnd we'll have a good time.\n\nNow, Maggie May has got it bad,\nThink she's lost her grip on reality.\nShe's gone to the doctor, and what did he say?\n\"Leave your worries behind, dear, you're 17.\"\n\nWell, we'll have a good time,\nAnd we'll have a good time,\nAnd we'll have a good time,\nAnd we'll have a good time.\n\nNow, Maggie May has got it bad,\nThink she's lost her grip on reality.\nShe's gone to the doctor, and what did he say?\n\"Leave your worries behind, dear, you're 17.\"\n\nWell, we'll have a good time,\nAnd we'll have a good time,\nAnd we'll have a good time,\nAnd we'll have a good time.\n\nNow, Maggie May has got it bad,\nThink she's lost her grip on reality.\nShe's gone to the doctor, and what did he say?\n\"Leave your worries behind, dear, you're 17.\"\n\nWell, we'll have a good time,\nAnd we'll have a good time,\nAnd we'll have a good time,\nAnd we'll have a good time.\n\nNow, Maggie May has got it bad,\nThink she's lost her grip on reality.\nShe's gone to the doctor, and what did he say?\n\"Leave your worries behind, dear, you're 17.\"\n\nWell, we'll have a good time,\nAnd we'll have a good time,\nAnd we'll hav