{"k": "f30fbe00606aa9603cf9ac08cd04e890", "t": "\nVerse 1:\nListen, I want to tell you something\nThe colors of my mind are flashing, see\nI'm trying to get used to this thing called freedom\nBut it's hard when all I do is dream\nOf being in a world where I belong\nWhere I can be myself and not feel so wrong\n\nChorus:\nPurple rain, purple rain\nGotta purify, gotta make it go away\nThe pain of the past, the shame and the fears\nGotta wash 'em away, gotta bring back the tears\n\nVerse 2:\nI'm trying to find my way through this darkest night\nBut I know that I can't do it alone, no fight\nI need someone to help me, someone to guide\nSomeone who'll stay by my side and be my bride\n\nChorus:\nPurple rain, purple rain\nGotta purify, gotta make it go away\nThe pain of the past, the shame and the fears\nGotta wash 'em away, gotta bring back the tears\n\nBridge:\nI'm standing in the rain, feeling so alone\nBut I know that I'm not, I have a home\nIn this world of confusion, where I don't belong\nI'll find my place, I'll make it strong\n\nChorus:\nPurple rain, purple rain\nGotta purify, gotta make it go away\nThe pain of the past, the shame and the fears\nGotta wash 'em away, gotta bring back the tears\n\nOutro:\nI'll never stop, I'll never give up the fight\nI'll keep on singing, until everything is alright\nPurple rain, purple rain, it's a new day to start\nAnd I'll be here, shining like a work of art."}
{"k": "465dffd7a727f5f3e362f1f3e818a32f", "t": "\nVerse 1:\nListen, I want to tell you something\nThe colors of my mind are flashing, see\nI'm trying to get used to this thing called freedom\nBut it's hard when all I do is dream\nOf being in a world where I belong\nWhere I can be myself and not feel so wrong\n\nChorus:\nPurple rain, purple rain\nGotta purify, gotta make it go away\nThe pain of the past, the shame and the fears\nGotta wash 'em away, gotta bring back the tears\n\nVerse 2:\nI'm trying to find my way through this darkest night\nBut I know that I can't do it alone, no fight\nI need someone to help me, someone to guide\nSomeone who'll stay by my side and be my bride\n\nChorus:\nPurple rain, purple rain\nGotta purify, gotta make it go away\nThe pain of the past, the shame and the fears\nGotta wash 'em away, gotta bring back the tears\n\nBridge:\nI'm standing in the rain, feeling so alone\nBut I know that I'm not, I have a home\nIn this world of confusion, where I don't belong\nI'll find my place, I'll make it strong\n\nChorus:\nPurple rain, purple rain\nGotta purify, gotta make it go away\nThe pain of the past, the shame and the fears\nGotta wash 'em away, gotta bring back the tears\n\nOutro:\nI'll never stop, I'll never give up the fight\nI'll keep on singing, until everything is alright\nPurple rain, purple rain, it's a new day to start\nAnd I'll be here, shining like a work of art."}
