{"k": "1016e4cedc4b8872af20a317bb31d069", "t": "Sure, here are the lyrics to \"Superstition\" by Stevie Wonder:\n\n(Verse 1)\nWhen you believe in things that you don't understand\nThen you suffer\nSuperstition ain't the way\n(Chorus)\nSuperstition ain't the way\nLookin' back on when I was a child\nMy mother would always say\n\"You'll find love and peace of mind\nWhen you believe in things that you don't understand\"\nBut now as I've grown older\nI'm not sure if I still believe it's true\n(Verse 2)\nAnd if you're left with just a feeling\nThat you can't explain\nJust remember that superstition ain't the way\n(Chorus)\nSuperstition ain't the way\nLookin' back on when I was a child\nMy mother would always say\n\"You'll find love and peace of mind\nWhen you believe in things that you don't understand\"\nBut now as I've grown older\nI'm not sure if I still believe it's true\n(Bridge)\nAnd even though I've tried to change\nThe way I feel inside\nI can't seem to break the chain\nOf superstition and pride\n(Chorus)\nSuperstition ain't the way\nLookin' back on when I was a child\nMy mother would always say\n\"You'll find love and peace of mind\nWhen you believe in things that you don't understand\"\nBut now as I've grown older\nI'm not sure if I still believe it's true\n(Outro)\nSuperstition ain't the way\nIt's just a superstition\nAnd it's keeping me up at night\nOh, superstition ain't the way."}
