{"k": "d56236d2c65856d7ad55f32ccbd5ac80", "t": "Sure, here are the lyrics to \"Born to Run\" by Bruce Springsteen:\n\nVerse 1:\nI wanna die with you Wendy on the streets tonight\nIn an everlasting kiss, in an endless night\nI'll race you to the bus stop, Wendy, I'll win every time\nAnd I'll love you till the end of time\n\nChorus:\nBorn to run, born to run\nGonna leave this town and never come back again\nBorn to run, born to run\nGonna find my own way, gonna make my own tracks\n\nVerse 2:\nWendy, Wendy, I wanna talk to you\nI wanna tell you something, but I don't know what to say\nI've been running around this town, trying to find my way\nBut I keep on running, and I never find the day\n\nChorus:\nBorn to run, born to run\nGonna leave this town and never come back again\nBorn to run, born to run\nGonna find my own way, gonna make my own tracks\n\nBridge:\nI'll take you down to the river, Wendy, and we'll watch the sun go down\nAnd I'll tell you all about my dreams, and how they've been getting bigger since the day I was born\nWe'll ride the river, Wendy, until the morning light\nAnd I'll love you till the end of time\n\nChorus:\nBorn to run, born to run\nGonna leave this town and never come back again\nBorn to run, born to run\nGonna find my own way, gonna make my own tracks"}
