{"k": "8300efb61e0565476a59183c744148a1", "t": "Here are the lyrics to \"Born to Run\" by Bruce Springsteen:\n\nIn the day we'll get it on\nAnd in the night we'll be free\nTo run and hide and chase our tails\nYou know it's true, you know it's true\n\nHey, kid, let me tell you 'bout the midnight special\nThe highway's jammed with broken heroes\nOn a last-chance power drive\nWell, they're young and they're restless\nTheir allegiances are cheap\nAnd their two-bit dreams are gonna leave 'em flat\nIt's up to you, you know it's true\n\nBorn to run\nBorn to run\nYou ain't got nothin' but your shadow when the sun goes down\nYou ain't got nothin' but your hunger when the night has come\nYou're born to run\n\nTramps like us, baby we were born to run\nWe gotta get out of this place\nIf we don't get some kicks before we go\nWe might as well be sleeping\nAnd I'll take you down the highway\nWhere the moon is shining bright\nAnd the stars are all aligned\nAnd we'll ride 'til the morning light\n\nBorn to run\nBorn to run\nYou ain't got nothin' but your shadow when the sun goes down\nYou ain't got nothin' but your hunger when the night has come\nYou're born to run\n\nTramps like us, baby we were born to run\nWe gotta get out of this place\nIf we don't get some kicks before we go\nWe might as well be sleeping\nAnd I'll take you down the highway\nWhere the moon is shining bright\nAnd the stars are all aligned\nAnd we'll ride 'til the morning light\n\nBorn to run\nBorn to run\nYou ain't got nothin' but your shadow when the sun goes down\nYou ain't got nothin' but your hunger when the night has come\nYou're born to run"}
{"k": "a06eb147ea4987ed286555a6986319dd", "t": "Here are the lyrics to \"Born to Run\" by Bruce Springsteen:\n\nIn the day we'll get it on\nAnd in the night we'll be free\nTo run and hide and chase our tails\nYou know it's true, you know it's true\n\nHey, kid, let me tell you 'bout the midnight hour\nWhen the sun beats down upon my shoulder\nI'm stuck between a dream and a nightmare\nAnd I don't know which way to go\n\nBorn to run, born to run\nBorn to run, born to run\n\nIn the day we'll get it on\nAnd in the night we'll be free\nTo run and hide and chase our tails\nYou know it's true, you know it's true\n\nHey, kid, let me tell you 'bout the midnight hour\nWhen the sun beats down upon my shoulder\nI'm stuck between a dream and a nightmare\nAnd I don't know which way to go\n\nBorn to run, born to run\nBorn to run, born to run\n\nTramps like us, baby we were born to run\nWe're gonna make it if we try\nJust a city boy, born and raised in South Detroit\nHe took the midnight train going anywhere\n\nJust a city boy, born and raised in South Detroit\nHe took the midnight train going anywhere\n\nBorn to run, born to run\nBorn to run, born to run\n\nTramps like us, baby we were born to run\nWe're gonna make it if we try\nJust a city boy, born and raised in South Detroit\nHe took the midnight train going anywhere\n\nHey, kid, let me tell you 'bout the midnight hour\nWhen the sun beats down upon my shoulder\nI'm stuck between a dream and a nightmare\nAnd I don't know which way to go\n\nBorn to run, born to run\nBorn to run, born to run\n\nTramps like us, baby we were born to run\nWe're gonna make it if we try\nJust a city boy, born and raised in South Detroit\nHe took the midnight train going anywhere"}
