{"k": "d107c1df0aba54e7c469d29c7d784c89", "t": "Sure, here are the lyrics to \"Ain't No Mountain High Enough\" by Diana Ross:\n\nVerse 1:\nI was born in a poor man's shack, on the wrong side of the tracks\nBut I never let my dreams be dismissed, no way\nI had a vision, a vision of what I could be\nAnd I knew that I could make it, if I just believed\n\nChorus:\nAin't no mountain high enough, ain't no valley low enough\nAin't no river wide enough, to keep me from getting over\nTo the other side, where my heart and soul will be free\nI'll keep on climbing, till I reach the other side\n\nVerse 2:\nI had a dream, a dream of a world where love is blind\nWhere we don't see color, or religion, or creed\nWhere everyone is equal, and everyone is free\nAnd I know that dream will come true, someday\n\nChorus:\nAin't no mountain high enough, ain't no valley low enough\nAin't no river wide enough, to keep me from getting over\nTo the other side, where my heart and soul will be free\nI'll keep on climbing, till I reach the other side\n\nBridge:\nAnd if I have to climb it alone, I'll find a way\nI'll make it to the top, someday\nI won't stop until I get there, no matter what they say\nI'll keep on climbing, till I reach the other side\n\nChorus:\nAin't no mountain high enough, ain't no valley low enough\nAin't no river wide enough, to keep me from getting over\nTo the other side, where my heart and soul will be free\nI'll keep on climbing, till I reach the other side"}
