{"k": "f1d69bbe214b63dfc77dc67573485e05", "t": "\n(Verse 1)\nI woke up this mornin', my body felt weak\nAn' I couldn't move, my bones were breakin'\nI reached out for my guitar, but it was out of reach\nAn' I knew that I'd never be the same again\n\n(Chorus)\nHurt, hurt, the feelin' is real\nHurt, hurt, it's tearin' me apart\nI've been hurt, I've been left behind\nAn' I can't find my way, no matter how hard I try\n\n(Verse 2)\nI've been down that road, where the sun don't shine\nAn' I've seen things that I ain't never gonna forget\nI've been hurt, I've been used an' abused\nAn' I'm still here, but I ain't no fool\n\n(Chorus)\nHurt, hurt, the feelin' is real\nHurt, hurt, it's tearin' me apart\nI've been hurt, I've been left behind\nAn' I can't find my way, no matter how hard I try\n\n(Bridge)\nI wish that I was alone, but I ain't\nCause nothin' ever dies, it just transforms\nAn' I'm still here, but I ain't the same\nAn' I know that I'll never be the same again\n\n(Verse 3)\nI've been hurt, I've been broken an' bruised\nAn' I've been left to pick up the pieces of my life\nBut I won't give up, no matter what they say\nCause I know that I'll find a way, come what may\n\n(Chorus)\nHurt, hurt, the feelin' is real\nHurt, hurt, it's tearin' me apart\nI've been hurt, I've been left behind\nAn' I can't find my way, no matter how hard I try\n\n(Outro)\nSo if you see me lyin' here in the dust\nJust give me a little push, an' I'll come out of this\nI'll rise up, I'll take my stand\nAn' I'll"}
