{"k": "70c5d8ae0f5ae0d94d8e6e01fbef4283", "t": "Here is a passage from \"The Lord of the Rings: The Fellowship of the Ring\" by J.R.R. Tolkien:\n\n\"As they walked, the sun began to set over the hills and the air grew cool and fragrant with the scent of blooming heather. Frodo felt his spirits lift as the weight of the Ring Bearer began to ease; for a while, at least, he could forget the peril that lay ahead and simply enjoy the beauty of Middle-earth.\n\n'Look!' said Gandalf, pointing upwards. 'The stars are coming out! The Elves call this the \"Star-pearl\" - the moment when the world is bathed in the soft light of the evening star.'\n\nFrodo looked up, and indeed the sky was filled with a thousand twinkling points of light. He felt a sense of wonder and awe wash over him as he gazed out at the celestial display.\n\n'In this hour,' said Gandalf, 'we are not far from Rivendell. The Elves will be expecting us soon.'\n\nAs they walked on, Frodo noticed that the trees grew taller and the air grew sweeter still. He could hear the distant sound of running water, and his heart quickened with excitement.\n\n'What's that noise?' he asked Gandalf.\n\n'That is the Anduin,' said the wizard. 'The great river that flows from the Misty Mountains to the sea. We will follow its course for a while yet.'\n\nAs they rounded a bend in the path, Frodo caught sight of the river itself - a broad, shining ribbon of water that flowed lazily through the valley. He felt a sense of peace wash over him as he gazed out at the tranquil scene.\n\n'Look!' said Gandalf again, this time pointing to a figure standing on the far bank of the river. 'That is Elrond's messenger. He has come to guide us to Rivendell.'\n\nFrodo followed Gandalf's gaze and saw a tall, slender figure clad in white robes, standing motionless as if carved from stone. As they drew closer, Frodo saw that it was indeed an Elf-maiden, her long hair blowing gently in the breeze.\n\n'Welcome, Gandalf,' she said, her voice like music. 'I have been sent to guide you to Rivendell. The Lord Elrond awaits your coming.'\n\nGandalf nodded gravely and turned to Frodo. 'This is our destination,' he said. 'The Last Homely House of"}
