{"k": "f94d7300a424d84829859f112046e04a", "t": "Certainly! Here is a long passage from \"Harry Potter and the Prisoner of Azkaban\" by J.K. Rowling:\n\n\"The night was dark and stormy, the perfect setting for a visit to Hogsmeade. Harry leaned back in his seat on the Hogwarts Express, watching as the lights of the village twinkled through the rain-speckled windows. He was excited to be going to Hogsmeade - he had never been there before, and he had heard so much about it from Ron and Hermione.\n\nAs the train rumbled on, Harry's thoughts turned to Sirius Black. He couldn't stop thinking about the letter he had received just before Christmas, informing him that Black was innocent of the crime for which he had been imprisoned for twelve years. It was hard to believe - how could someone who had been convicted of murdering twelve people be innocent? And yet, there it was in black and white: Sirius Black was not the monster Harry had always believed him to be.\n\nHarry's mind raced with questions. Why had he been framed? Who had really killed the Muggles? And why had no one believed Black when he had claimed to be innocent all along? Harry felt a shiver run down his spine as he thought about how close he had come to being killed by the same person who had killed those twelve people.\n\nHe glanced around the train car, hoping to distract himself from his thoughts. Ron and Hermione were engrossed in a book, while Neville and Luna were deep in conversation. Ginny was reading a magazine, her long blonde hair cascading down her back like a golden waterfall. Harry felt a pang of envy - he wished he could be as carefree as they were, but he knew that his own worries would never truly disappear.\n\nAs the train pulled into Hogsmeade station, Harry stood up and gathered his belongings. He was eager to explore the village and find out more about Sirius Black. He had a feeling that this was just the beginning of a great adventure.\"\n\nI hope you enjoy this passage! Let me know if you have any other requests."}
