{"k": "b8eeffd2d5816c4005d1eff794009898", "t": "Here is a passage from \"Harry Potter and the Prisoner of Azkaban\":\n\n\"'You're not thinking fourth-dimensionally, Harry,' said Hermione, as they walked back to Gryffindor Tower on the first day of term.\n\n'What are you talking about?' asked Ron, looking at Hermione in confusion.\n\n'Hermione's got a point, though,' said Harry, his eyes fixed on the castle windows. 'If Sirius Black was trying to kill me, why didn't he just do it when I was with my parents? Why wait twelve years?'\n\n'Because he wasn't trying to kill you, that's why,' said Hermione, her voice firm. 'You're not thinking fourth-dimensionally, Harry.'\n\n'I am too thinking fourth-dimensionally!' said Harry, his face reddening.\n\n'Well, you're not doing it very well, then,' said Ron, grinning.\n\nHermione rolled her eyes. 'It's a simple concept, really. If Sirius Black was trying to kill you when you were a baby, he would have had to be in the same place as your parents at the same time. But if he was trying to get to you through time...'\n\n'Wait a minute,' said Harry, his eyes lighting up. 'You're saying that Sirius Black is trying to get to me from the future?'\n\nHermione nodded. 'Exactly! If he's been imprisoned in Azkaban for twelve years, and then suddenly breaks out... it's like he's coming back to the past to try and kill you.'\n\nHarry felt a shiver run down his spine. He had always known that Sirius Black was supposed to be trying to kill him, but this was different. This was like something out of a nightmare.\n\n'But why?' he asked, his voice barely above a whisper. 'Why would someone want to kill me?'\n\nHermione and Ron exchanged a look. 'We don't know yet,' said Hermione. 'But we're going to find out.'\n\nHarry nodded, feeling a sense of determination wash over him. He was going to get to the bottom of this mystery, no matter what it took.\"\n\nI hope you enjoyed that passage! Let me know if you have any other requests."}
