{"k": "46be92f22447c8b1a1d0ea9805e1d3b5", "t": "Here is a passage from Chapter 5 of \"The Lion, the Witch, and the Wardrobe\" by C.S. Lewis:\n\n\"As they walked, Lucy noticed that the trees grew taller and the air grew colder. She could see her breath misting in front of her face. 'It's getting very cold,' she said to Edmund.\n\n'Yes, it is,' he replied. 'I don't like this place at all.'\n\n'I don't either,' said Lucy. 'Let's go back.'\n\nBut before they could turn back, a figure appeared on the path ahead. It was a tall, thin woman with long silver hair and a face as white as snow. She was dressed in green and had a crown of holly on her head.\n\n'Ah, ah, ah,' she said, her voice like ice. 'What do we have here? A little girl from our world, I see. And you, young man - what are you doing with her?'\n\nLucy felt a shiver run down her spine as the woman's eyes fixed on her. She tried to speak, but her voice was stuck in her throat.\n\n'Who are you?' Edmund asked, trying to sound brave.\n\n'I am the White Witch,' she replied. 'And this is Narnia - my kingdom.'\n\nLucy felt a strange sensation, as if the air around her had grown colder still. She looked up at the Witch and saw that her eyes were fixed on her with an unnerving intensity.\n\n'What do you want?' Edmund asked again.\n\n'I want to know what you're doing here,' said the Witch. 'You're not from Narnia, are you?'\n\nLucy shook her head, trying to find her voice.\n\n'Then you have no business being here,' said the Witch. 'This is a place of eternal winter - and I am its queen.'\n\nAs she spoke, Lucy felt the air grow colder still. She could see her breath misting in front of her face, and she knew that if they stayed there much longer, they would freeze to death.\n\n'Let's go back,' she whispered to Edmund.\n\nBut before they could turn away, the Witch spoke again:\n\n'I'll give you a choice. You can either come with me and be my guests - or you can stay here and freeze to death.'\n\nLucy knew that they had to get out of there as quickly as possible. She took Edmund's hand and pulled him along the path, trying to get away from the Witch as fast as she could.\"\n\n"}
