at cannot be described by our normal laws of physics.\n\nThe singularity is often referred to as the 'Big Bang'. It is a misleading name, because it implies that there was a bang, a sudden explosion, at some point in the past. But this is not what happened. The universe did not have a beginning; it simply has always existed. The Big Bang was just an event, a moment when the universe began to expand and cool down. It is a moment that we can never observe directly, because our clocks would run backwards if we went back in time to"}
