{"k": "81e04c088929a8ac19a6d51173930a04", "t": "Here's a passage from \"Rich Dad Poor Dad\" by Robert Kiyosaki:\n\n\"The main reason most people struggle financially is that they have been taught that it's wrong to be rich. They have been taught that money is the root of all evil, and that wealth is something to be ashamed of. This is a lie.\n\nMy poor dad was a well-educated man who had a good job and earned a comfortable income. He was proud of his education and his job, but he was not wealthy. In fact, he struggled financially throughout his life because he did not understand the difference between being rich and being wealthy.\n\nBeing rich means having a lot of money, but it does not necessarily mean that you are wealthy. Being wealthy means having financial freedom, which is different from just having a lot of money. Financial freedom means that you have enough money to do what you want, when you want, without worrying about how you will pay your bills.\n\nMy rich dad was a high school dropout who had no formal education. He did not earn a good income, but he was wealthy because he understood the difference between being rich and being wealthy. He knew that financial freedom was more important than just having a lot of money.\n\nThe main reason my poor dad struggled financially is that he did not understand the concept of passive income. Passive income is income that you earn without actively working for it. For example, if you own rental property, you can earn passive income from the rent that your tenants pay. If you have stocks or bonds, you can earn passive income from the dividends or interest they pay.\n\nMy poor dad worked hard his whole life and earned a good income, but he did not understand how to create passive income. He was stuck in a cycle of working for money, rather than having money work for him. This is why he struggled financially throughout his life.\n\nOn the other hand, my rich dad understood the concept of passive income. He knew that it was possible to earn money without actively working for it, and he made sure to create passive income streams in his financial portfolio. This is why he was able to achieve financial freedom and live a wealthy lifestyle.\n\nThe main lesson I learned from my poor dad is that financial education is important. My poor dad had a good job and earned a comfortable income, but he did not understand the basics of personal finance. He did not know how to create passive income or how to invest his money wisely.\n\nOn the other hand, my rich dad was financially educated. He knew how to create passive income and how"}
