   min = j\n        swap(A[i], A[min])\n\n```\n\nThis algorithm also has a time complexity of O(n^2), which makes it inefficient for large arrays. However, like insertion sort, it is simple to implement and can be useful in certain situations where the array is small or partially sorted.\n\nIn the next chapter, we will explore more advanced sorting algorithms that have better time complexities than these two methods. We"}
