 way. You then get this MVP in front of real customers as quickly as possible, either through a landing page or by offering it for free to a small group of early adopters.\n\nAs the customers start using your service, you learn what they like and don't like about it. You might discover that some users are confused by certain features, while others love the simplicity of the interface. You use this feedback to iterate on the product, making changes and improvements based on what you've learned.\n\nThis process continues until you have a product that is truly valuable to your customers. And even then, you don't stop learning. You continue to gather feedback and make adjustments as"}
