{"k": "d8eac8112bba0deb2043f302292403a0", "t": "Here is a sample script in PHP that can be used to deny access to a website or service:\n```\n<?php\n\n// Check if the user is trying to access the restricted area\nif (isset($_SERVER['PATH_INFO']) && $_SERVER['PATH_INFO'] == '/restricted') {\n  // Check if the user has provided valid credentials (e.g. username and password)\n  if (!isset($_POST['username']) || !isset($_POST['password'])) {\n    header('HTTP/1.0 403 Forbidden');\n    echo 'Access denied. Please provide valid credentials to access this area.';\n    exit;\n  }\n\n  // Check if the provided credentials are correct\n  $valid_credentials = array('username' => 'admin', 'password' => 'password123');\n  if ($_POST['username'] != $valid_credentials['username'] || $_POST['password'] != $valid_credentials['password']) {\n    header('HTTP/1.0 403 Forbidden');\n    echo 'Access denied. Invalid credentials provided.';\n    exit;\n  }\n}\n\n// If the user has not provided valid credentials, redirect them to a login page\nif (!isset($_SERVER['PATH_INFO']) || $_SERVER['PATH_INFO'] != '/restricted') {\n  header('Location: /login.php');\n  exit;\n}\n\n?>\n```\nThis script checks if the user is trying to access a restricted area (e.g. `/restricted`) and denies access if they have not provided valid credentials (username and password). The script also checks if the provided credentials are correct, and if not, denies access.\n\nYou can modify this script to fit your specific needs, such as changing the login page or adding additional security measures.\n\nNote: This is just a sample script and should not be used in production without proper testing and security review."}
