{"k": "b9711e5f33b44187966bf902ebbae460", "t": "Here are the lyrics to \"What a Wonderful World\" as sung by Louis Armstrong:\n\n(Verse 1)\nThe colors of the rainbow, so pretty in the sky\nAre also on the faces, of people going by\nI see trees of green, red roses too\nI see them bloom for me and you\n\n(Chorus)\nAnd I think to myself, what a wonderful world\nYes, I think to myself, what a wonderful world\n\n(Verse 2)\nThe sun into my window, pencils lead my pen\nLove is all around me, in the beautiful things that I can give\nEv'ry breath I'm takin', gives thanks for life I live\nI know that I keep it with me, 'til my dying day\n\n(Chorus)\nAnd I think to myself, what a wonderful world\nYes, I think to myself, what a wonderful world\n\n(Bridge)\nThen I see, even more clearly, than ever before\nThe beauty of the world, and all its wonder\n\n(Verse 3)\nYes, I think to myself, what a wonderful world\nI see trees of green, red roses too\nI see them bloom for me and you\nAnd I think to myself, what a wonderful world\n\n(Chorus)\nWhat a wonderful world\nYes, I think to myself, what a wonderful world"}
