{"k": "15aad8eeb3c9ddd6786905d57bba6c05", "t": "Here are the lyrics to \"Gimme Shelter\" by The Rolling Stones:\n\nWar, children, it's just a shot away\nIt's just a shot away\nWar, children, it's just a shot away\nIt's just a shelter\n\nOh, a storm is threatening my very life today\nIf I don't get some shelter, oh yeah, I'm gonna fade away\nWar, children, it's just a shot away\nIt's just a shot away\n\nWhoa, oh, oh, whoa, oh, oh\nGimme shelter, oh, oh, oh, oh\nGimme shelter, my friend, my friend\n\nOh, a storm is threatening my very life today\nIf I don't get some shelter, oh yeah, I'm gonna fade away\nWar, children, it's just a shot away\nIt's just a shot away\n\nWhoa, oh, oh, whoa, oh, oh\nGimme shelter, oh, oh, oh, oh\nGimme shelter, my friend, my friend\n\nOh, a storm is threatening my very life today\nIf I don't get some shelter, oh yeah, I'm gonna fade away\nWar, children, it's just a shot away\nIt's just a shot away\n\nWhoa, oh, oh, whoa, oh, oh\nGimme shelter, oh, oh, oh, oh\nGimme shelter, my friend, my friend\n\nNote: These are the original lyrics as they appear on the 1969 album \"Let It Bleed\". There may be slight variations in different live performances or covers of the song."}
