{"k": "3d9b0ef634edd0728acaa06c773dff7d", "t": "Here are the lyrics to \"American Pie\" by Don McLean:\n\nVerse 1:\nA long, long time ago\nI can still remember how\nThat music used to make me smile\nAnd I knew if I had my chance\nWell, then you'd see me walking in a crowd\nBy now you know what I'm not proud of\n\nChorus:\nTo be sure that is sad\nNever meaning to cause you sorrow\nI never meant to cause you pain\nLet this be a lesson to you all\nYour old ideas are retro\nAnd your new ideas are the blues\n\nVerse 2:\nWhere do we go from here?\nThe day the music died\nAnd while Lenin read a book on Marx\nThe quartet practiced in the park\nAnd we were singing, Fiddlin' and faddin'\nWith the lights out, it's less dangerous\n\nChorus:\nTo be sure that is sad\nNever meaning to cause you sorrow\nI never meant to cause you pain\nLet this be a lesson to you all\nYour old ideas are retro\nAnd your new ideas are the blues\n\nVerse 3:\nNow for ten years we've been on our own\nAnd moss grows fat on a roll of cheese\nStrummin' my pick and singin' my song\nWe were singin', \"Bye, bye, Miss American Pie\"\nDrove my Chevy to the levee\nBut the levee was dry\n\nChorus:\nTo be sure that is sad\nNever meaning to cause you sorrow\nI never meant to cause you pain\nLet this be a lesson to you all\nYour old ideas are retro\nAnd your new ideas are the blues\n\nVerse 4:\nA hard rain's gonna fall\nAnd when the sky was filled with smoke\nAnd every little bird flew out of its nest\nFor no one knew then who the clown and the fool were\nBut now it's all too clear to see\nYou can't write a song about yesterday\n\nChorus:\nTo be sure that is sad\nNever meaning to cause you sorrow\nI never meant to cause you pain\nLet this be a lesson to you all\nYour old ideas are retro\nAnd your new ideas are the blues\n\nVerse 5:\nThe jester sang for the king and queen\nIn a coat he borrowed from James Dean\nAnd a voice that came from you and me\nOh, and while Lenin read a book on Marx\nThe quartet practiced in the park\nAnd we were singing, Fiddlin"}
