{"k": "d5e41c20d15b1f9e8e58bb0425395074", "t": "Here are the lyrics to \"Uptown Girl\" by Billy Joel:\n\nShe's been living in her uptown world\nI would never have asked for\nBut you don't know what it's like\nShe's been living in her uptown world\nI would never have asked for\n\nIt was gypsy blood that she had made me crave\nAnd I could wait forever, and all through the night\nBut I'll be lucky if she gives me a sign\nThat she wants to see me tonight\n\nWell, we keep comfortable with our money and our cars\nAnd watered down our troubles in a foreign star\nShe's been living in her uptown world\nI would never have asked for\n\nIt was gypsy blood that she had made me crave\nAnd I could wait forever, and all through the night\nBut I'll be lucky if she gives me a sign\nThat she wants to see me tonight\n\nWell, we keep comfortable with our money and our cars\nAnd watered down our troubles in a foreign star\nShe's been living in her uptown world\nI would never have asked for\n\nIt was gypsy blood that she had made me crave\nAnd I could wait forever, and all through the night\nBut I'll be lucky if she gives me a sign\nThat she wants to see me tonight\n\n(Note: These are the original lyrics as they appear on the 1983 album \"An Innocent Man\". There may be slight variations in different versions or live performances of the song.)"}
