{"k": "a6e0b8b089cdd7235a370ede8a0f85b1", "t": "I'm happy to help! However, I need to correct you - \"Smooth\" is not a song by Santana. The song \"Smooth\" is actually a collaboration between Rob Thomas (of Matchbox Twenty) and Santana.\n\nHere are the lyrics to \"Smooth\":\n\nVerbal sparks fly from my fingertips\nUnbelievable, the way I make 'em scatter\nThe rhythm's got me feeling like a star\nI'm on a roll, and it's getting harder\n\nTo get to you, gotta get to you\nGotta get to you, gotta get to you\n\nYou're so fine, you blow my mind\nHey, baby, here's my number, call me anytime\nYou're so fine, you blow my mind\nHey, baby, here's my number, call me anytime\n\nI'm feeling smooth, yeah, I'm feeling smooth\nGot the spotlight on me and it feels like a dream\nI'm feeling smooth, yeah, I'm feeling smooth\nGot the spotlight on me and it feels like a dream\n\nYou're so fine, you blow my mind\nHey, baby, here's my number, call me anytime\nYou're so fine, you blow my mind\nHey, baby, here's my number, call me anytime\n\nI'm feeling smooth, yeah, I'm feeling smooth\nGot the spotlight on me and it feels like a dream\nI'm feeling smooth, yeah, I'm feeling smooth\nGot the spotlight on me and it feels like a dream\n\nSantana's guitar work is featured prominently throughout the song, with Rob Thomas' vocals adding a pop-rock flair. The song was released in 1999 as part of Santana's album \"Supernatural\" and became a huge hit, winning three Grammy Awards including Record of the Year."}
