{"k": "471ad64c78424ebbfa8c44a71044f61f", "t": "Here are the lyrics to \"Pinball Wizard\" from The Who's 1969 rock opera album \"Tommy\":\n\n**Verse 1 (Sally Simpson)**\nHe makes me laugh with the things he says\nTo me, he's just a pinball machine\nHis fingers snap like they're pinballs\nWhen he plays the machines\n\n**Chorus (Pinball Wizard)**\nHe's a pinball wizard, there has to be a twist behind\nHe may look small but he thinks big\nThat deaf, dumb and blind kid sure plays a mean pinball\n\n**Verse 2 (Sally Simpson)**\nHe's got an extra ball in the air\nAnd another one coming up\nHe's got the high score, he's number one\nYou'd think that he'd be careful with his fingers\n\n**Chorus (Pinball Wizard)**\nHe's a pinball wizard, there has to be a twist behind\nHe may look small but he thinks big\nThat deaf, dumb and blind kid sure plays a mean pinball\n\n**Bridge (Sally Simpson)**\nI'm not the pinball king, no sirree\nBut I can play that machine like nobody's business\nI've got the skills, I've got the flair\nI'll show you how it's done, I don't care!\n\n**Chorus (Pinball Wizard)**\nHe's a pinball wizard, there has to be a twist behind\nHe may look small but he thinks big\nThat deaf, dumb and blind kid sure plays a mean pinball\n\nNote: These are the original lyrics as they appear on the \"Tommy\" album. There may be slight variations in different live performances or covers of the song."}
