{"k": "f69650512312f0732bc6533712b2f0dc", "t": "Here are the lyrics to \"Maggie May\" by Rod Stewart:\n\nI was young and easy under the sun\nNow same time, next year\nBut another day, another dollar, another woman, another fight\nAnd I'm getting older too\n\nYou could have done anything, Maggie may\nWhy'd you choose that old man to marry?\nYou knew how much beloved he'd be\n'Cause when he came out of the door, the girls all screamed Maggie May\n\nI was young and easy under the sun\nNow same time, next year\nBut another day, another dollar, another woman, another fight\nAnd I'm getting older too\n\nYou could have done anything, Maggie may\nWhy'd you choose that old man to marry?\nYou knew how much beloved he'd be\n'Cause when he came out of the door, the girls all screamed Maggie May\n\nI was young and easy under the sun\nNow same time, next year\nBut another day, another dollar, another woman, another fight\nAnd I'm getting older too\n\nYou could have done anything, Maggie may\nWhy'd you choose that old man to marry?\nYou knew how much beloved he'd be\n'Cause when he came out of the door, the girls all screamed Maggie May"}
