{"k": "0ae08f3dca8fdccbef56e51b742f0ed1", "t": "Here are the lyrics to \"Killer Queen\" by Queen:\n\nIs this the real life? Is this just fantasy?\nCaught in a landslide, no escape from reality\nOpen your eyes, look up to the skies and see\nI'm just a poor boy, I need no sympathy\n\nBecause I'm easy come, easy go, little high, little low\nAny way the wind blows doesn't really matter to me\nMama, oooh (any way the wind blows)\n\nMama, oooh (any way the wind blows)\nMama, oooh (any way the wind blows)\n\nI'm a killer queen, marching to the beat of a different drum\nNo one else can recommend you for me\nSomebody save me, somebody save me\n\nAny way the wind blows doesn't really matter to me\nMama, oooh (any way the wind blows)\nMama, oooh (any way the wind blows)\n\nI'm a killer queen, marching to the beat of a different drum\nNo one else can recommend you for me\nSomebody save me, somebody save me\n\nAny way the wind blows doesn't really matter to me\nMama, oooh (any way the  wind blows)\nMama, oooh (any way the wind blows)\n\nNote: These are the original lyrics as they appear on the album \"Sheer Heart Attack\" (1974). There may be slight variations in different versions or live performances of the song."}
