{"k": "1e3a3404b11290a0a5e0ef897b6f889d", "t": "Here are the lyrics to \"Black Magic Woman\" by Santana:\n\n(Verse 1)\nGypsy, lord and master\nAll our children's dreams\nYou know just what it is\nTo make us use them\n\n(Chorus)\nOh, black magic woman\nMy Bambi doll\nYou know just what it is\nAnd I feel that you're mine\n\n(Verse 2)\nGypsy, lord and master\nAll our children's dreams\nYou know just what it is\nTo make us use them\n\n(Chorus)\nOh, black magic woman\nMy Bambi doll\nYou know just what it is\nAnd I feel that you're mine\n\n(Bridge)\nI believe in all the things you do\nI believe in all the things you say\nI believe in all the things you do\nI believe in all the things you say\n\n(Chorus)\nOh, black magic woman\nMy Bambi doll\nYou know just what it is\nAnd I feel that you're mine\n\nNote: These are the original lyrics as written by Fleetwood Mac (Peter Green) and recorded by Santana. The song was later covered by Fleetwood Mac in 1971 with Stevie Nicks on vocals, but these are the original lyrics."}
