{"k": "5909f347a61ac424a92d94e1914c3034", "t": "Here are the lyrics to \"Superstition\" by Stevie Wonder:\n\nWhen you believe in things that you don't understand\nThen you should not stand afraid\nJust 'cause you feel like a number doesn't mean you ain't got soul\nAnd when I feel down, and my back is turned around\nI'm gonna keep on tryin', till I get it right\n\nSuperstition, oh, oh, oh\nSuperstition, oh, oh, oh\nDon't let the devil take control of your mind\nDon't let the devil take control of your mind\n\nWhen you're ridin' high, and you're feelin' fine\nAnd you think that you've got it made\nBut then you fall, and you hit the floor\nAnd you wonder why, and you ask for more\n\nSuperstition, oh, oh, oh\nSuperstition, oh, oh, oh\nDon't let the devil take control of your mind\nDon't let the devil take control of your mind\n\nWhen you're ridin' high, and you're feelin' fine\nAnd you think that you've got it made\nBut then you fall, and you hit the floor\nAnd you wonder why, and you ask for more\n\nSuperstition, oh, oh, oh\nSuperstition, oh, oh, oh\nDon't let the devil take control of your mind\nDon't let the devil take control of your mind\n\n(Repeat to fade)\n\nNote: These are the original lyrics as they appear on Stevie Wonder's 1972 album \"Talking Book\"."}
