{"k": "b795a7de6270522fb9e6057c2d784dd5", "t": "Here are the lyrics to \"Superstition\" by Stevie Wonder:\n\nWhen you believe in things that you don't understand\nThen you suffer\nSuperstition ain't the way\n\nOh, have you considered the possibility?\nThat there's something here that time won't erase?\nI'm gonna find out for myself\nSo I can show my friends back home\n\nSuperstition, oh superstition\nYou're a wicked thing\nWhen you believe in things that you don't understand\nThen you suffer\nSuperstition ain't the way\n\nOh, have you considered the possibility?\nThat there's something here that time won't erase?\nI'm gonna find out for myself\nSo I can show my friends back home\n\nYou know it's just a superstition\nWhen you believe in things that you don't understand\nThen you suffer\nSuperstition ain't the way\n\nOh, have you considered the possibility?\nThat there's something here that time won't erase?\nI'm gonna find out for myself\nSo I can show my friends back home\n\n(Note: These are the original lyrics as they appear on Stevie Wonder's 1972 album \"Talking Book\". There may be slight variations in different versions or live performances of the song.)"}
