{"k": "341fe5aa6695287da9439e2ce57763e5", "t": "Here are the lyrics to \"Rocket Man\" by Elton John:\n\n**Verse 1**\nShe packed my bags last night, pre-flight\nZero hour, nine a.m.\nAnd I'm gonna be high as a kite by then\nI miss the earth so much, I miss my wife\n\n**Chorus**\nIt's lonely out in space\nOn such a timeless flight\nAnd I think it's gonna be a long, long time\nBefore I ever get this chance again\n\n**Verse 2**\nPropane kitchens and air-to-air missiles\nI put my suit on, quick before they close the sky\nI'm floating in a most peculiar way\nAnd the stars look very different today\n\n**Chorus**\nIt's lonely out in space\nOn such a timeless flight\nAnd I think it's gonna be a long, long time\nBefore I ever get this chance again\n\n**Bridge**\nFor here am I sitting in a tin can\nFar above the world\nPlanet earth is blue and there's nothing I can do\n\n**Chorus**\nThough I'm a rocket man\nFlying in a tin can\nBut if they ask me what I like to see\nI'll say \"Fly me to the moon\"\n\n**Outro**\nAnd let me play among the stars\nLet me see what spring is like\nThen tell me no one's laughing when I say\nThat I'm a rocket man\n\nNote: These are the original lyrics as written by Bernie Taupin and Elton John. There may be slight variations in different versions or live performances of the song."}
