{"k": "08224bb55221e96dd909cbb8db300cc1", "t": "Here are the lyrics to \"Burning Down the House\" by Talking Heads:\n\nYou may be a dreamer\nOf the dark and violent times\nOr a returning king\nWith some newfangled scheme\n\nYou may be a road worker\nFrame by frame\nYou may be a man of science\nOr a man of war\n\nYou may be a danger zone\nA radioactive night\nYou may be a red door\nA pretty good year\n\nYou may be a one or the other\nBut whatever you are\nWhatever you've got\nI can show you something better than a dream\n\nYou may be a dreamer\nOf the dark and violent times\nOr a returning king\nWith some newfangled scheme\n\nYou may be a road worker\nFrame by frame\nYou may be a man of science\nOr a man of war\n\nYou may be a danger zone\nA radioactive night\nYou may be a red door\nA pretty good year\n\nYou may be a one or the other\nBut whatever you are\nWhatever you've got\nI can show you something better than a dream\n\n(Note: These are the original lyrics as they appear on the 1983 album \"Speaking in Tongues\". There may be slight variations in different versions or live performances of the song.)"}
