{"k": "c5ba88189c2ccb30d669d58264bbe7e7", "t": "Here are the lyrics to \"Born to Run\" by Bruce Springsteen:\n\nNow, here he came from down the block\nHe said, \"Son, I want to know if this is the place\nWhere nothing ever happens past this old red line\nI just got to get away\"\n\nWell, we'll make it, I said, \"We'll have a good time\nJust you and me, baby, we'll find our own paradise\"\nHe said, \"Now, when you're out there on that highway\nBetter not stop for nothin', boy, better fuel up in your tank\nAnd keep her full of gas, don't be slowin' down\"\n\nHold on to sixteen as long as you can\nChange it with seventeen and drive all night\nThey got a lot of empty pages in this old town\nYou got a lot of empty pages in your head\n\nNow, here he came from down the block\nHe said, \"Son, I want to know if this is the place\nWhere nothing ever happens past this old red line\nI just got to get away\"\n\nWell, we'll make it, I said, \"We'll have a good time\nJust you and me, baby, we'll find our own paradise\"\nHe said, \"Now, when you're out there on that highway\nBetter not stop for nothin', boy, better fuel up in your tank\nAnd keep her full of gas, don't be slowin' down\"\n\nYou ain't a boy, you got to grow up now\nBut why they got to teach us 'specially the ones who can't learn?\nThey've got everything that we need\nYou ain't a boy, you got to grow up now\n\nNow, here he came from down the block\nHe said, \"Son, I want to know if this is the place\nWhere nothing ever happens past this old red line\nI just got to get away\"\n\nWell, we'll make it, I said, \"We'll have a good time\nJust you and me, baby, we'll find our own paradise\"\nHe said, \"Now, when you're out there on that highway\nBetter not stop for nothin', boy, better fuel up in your tank\nAnd keep her full of gas, don't be slowin' down\"\n\nYou can look the other way\nWe'll make it, I said, \"We'll have a good time\nJust you and me, baby, we'll find our own paradise\"\nHe said, \""}
{"k": "6d48239682e5795dbe1ebf15c8005b0b", "t": "Here are the lyrics to \"Born to Run\" by Bruce Springsteen:\n\nNow, here he came from down the block\nHe said, \"Son, I want to know if this is the place\nWhere nothing ever happens past this old red line\nI just got to get away\"\n\nWell, we'll make it, I said, \"We'll have a good time\nJust you and me, baby, we'll find our own paradise\"\nHe said, \"Now, when you're out there on that highway\nBetter not stop for nothin', boy, better fuel up in your tank\nAnd keep her full of gas, don't be slowin' down\"\n\nHold on to sixteen as long as you can\nChange it with seventeen and drive all night\nThey got a lot of empty pages in this old town\nYou got a lot of empty pages in your head\n\nNow, here he came from down the block\nHe said, \"Son, I want to know if this is the place\nWhere nothing ever happens past this old red line\nI just got to get away\"\n\nWell, we'll make it, I said, \"We'll have a good time\nJust you and me, baby, we'll find our own paradise\"\nHe said, \"Now, when you're out there on that highway\nBetter not stop for nothin', boy, better fuel up in your tank\nAnd keep her full of gas, don't be slowin' down\"\n\nYou ain't a boy, you got to grow up now\nBut why they got to teach us 'specially the ones who can't learn?\nThey've got everything that we need\nYou ain't a boy, you got to grow up now\n\nNow, here he came from down the block\nHe said, \"Son, I want to know if this is the place\nWhere nothing ever happens past this old red line\nI just got to get away\"\n\nWell, we'll make it, I said, \"We'll have a good time\nJust you and me, baby, we'll find our own paradise\"\nHe said, \"Now, when you're out there on that highway\nBetter not stop for nothin', boy, better fuel up in your tank\nAnd keep her full of gas, don't be slowin' down\"\n\nYou can look the other way\nWe'll make it, I said, \"We'll have a good time\nJust you and me, baby, we'll find our own paradise\"\nHe said, \""}
