{"k": "1276360371d16f0c0396da514e808c34", "t": "Here are the lyrics to \"Ain't No Mountain High Enough\" by Diana Ross:\n\nThere ain't no mountain high enough\nNo valley low enough\nBut I know a place where we can go\nAnd be just you and me, baby\n\nWe'll have our own world there\nWhere nobody else will ever roam\nJust you and me, baby\n\nAin't no river wide enough\nI won't hesitate no more\nNo valley too steep\nTo make the feelings that I got for you, real\n\nThere ain't no mountain high enough\nNo valley low enough\nBut I know a place where we can go\nAnd be just you and me, baby\n\nWe'll have our own world there\nWhere nobody else will ever roam\nJust you and me, baby\n\nAin't no river wide enough\nI won't hesitate no more\nNo valley too steep\nTo make the feelings that I got for you, real\n\nThere ain't no mountain high enough\nNo valley low enough\nBut I know a place where we can go\nAnd be just you and me, baby\n\nWe'll have our own world there\nWhere nobody else will ever roam\nJust you and me, baby"}
