{"k": "a9cdd3c864befa7ce05fd85e4da7808c", "t": "Here are the lyrics to \"Under the Bridge\" by Red Hot Chili Peppers:\n\n[Verse 1]\nI guess I just was meant to tell you\nApothecaries' children at the beauty parlor\nDrivin'\nYou know they say he's from Illinois\nHis skin is a special brown\n\n[Chorus]\nHere we go, dump the body in the lake\nWell, the water flows around her brain\nHere we go, pull the plug, here we go\nAnd I don't ever want to feel like I did that day\n\n[Verse 2]\nI put my hand out, broke the window and had some fun\nAnd then the fog was rising from the trees\nAnd it was all so pretty, my god how the seconds fly\nYou know they say he's from Illinois\n\n[Chorus]\nHere we go, dump the body in the lake\nWell, the water flows around her brain\nHere we go, pull the plug, here we go\nAnd I don't ever want to feel like I did that day\n\n[Bridge]\nI'd like to bathe in the brine of your tears\nBut they washed away and were gone when I woke up\nIt's something unpredictable, but in the end it's right\nI hope you had the time of your life\n\n[Chorus]\nHere we go, dump the body in the lake\nWell, the water flows around her brain\nHere we go, pull the plug, here we go\nAnd I don't ever want to feel like I did that day\n\n[Outro]\nSometimes I feel like I don't have a partner\nGold dust woman and men love it when you lend an ear\nI'm not big on social norms, so any thing goes\nBut me, I wish I could sleep in till the end.\n\nNote: These are the original lyrics as they appear on the album \"Blood Sugar Sex Magik\". There may be slight variations in different versions or live performances of the song."}
{"k": "86dfbae8dcd5fcddd7079b6170a8184f", "t": "Here are the lyrics to \"Under the Bridge\" by Red Hot Chili Peppers:\n\n[Verse 1]\nI guess I just was meant to tell you\nApothecaries' children at the beauty parlor\nDrivin'\nYou know they say he's from Illinois\nHis skin is a special brown\n\n[Chorus]\nHere we go, dump the body in the lake\nWell, the water flows around her brain\nHere we go, pull the plug, here we go\nAnd I don't ever want to feel like I did that day\n\n[Verse 2]\nI put my hand out, broke the window and had some fun\nAnd then the fog was rising from the trees\nAnd it was all so pretty, my god how the seconds fly\nYou know they say he's from Illinois\n\n[Chorus]\nHere we go, dump the body in the lake\nWell, the water flows around her brain\nHere we go, pull the plug, here we go\nAnd I don't ever want to feel like I did that day\n\n[Bridge]\nI'd like to bathe in the brine of your tears\nBut they washed away and were gone when I woke up\nIt's something unpredictable, but in the end it's right\nI hope you had the time of your life\n\n[Chorus]\nHere we go, dump the body in the lake\nWell, the water flows around her brain\nHere we go, pull the plug, here we go\nAnd I don't ever want to feel like I did that day\n\n[Outro]\nSometimes I feel like I don't have a partner\nGold dust woman and men love it when you lend an ear\nI'm not big on social norms, so any thing goes\nBut me, I wish I could sleep in till the end.\n\nNote: These are the original lyrics as they appear on the album \"Blood Sugar Sex Magik\". There may be slight variations in different versions or live performances of the song."}
