{"k": "1c7ecc780c037cfed2150efcb254cd03", "t": "Here are the lyrics to \"Hurt\" by Johnny Cash:\n\nI hurt myself today\nTo see if I still feel\nI focus on the pain\nThe only thing that's real\n\nThe kind you breathe\n\nI was a blind man\nAt the bottom of a well\nLooking up at the sky\nBut it's so dark coming down\n\nIt's so hard when nothing goes right\nForgive myself, but it's all I can do\n\nI hurt myself today\nTo see if I still feel\nI focus on the pain\nThe only thing that's real\n\nThe kind you breathe\n\nWhat have I become, my sweetest friend?\nWhy am I so alone, I know why everyone goes away\n\nI've seen the needle and the damage done\nBut it's my own fault, it's my own fault\n\nMy body's here but you're gone\nKnow what any emotional pain can do to your mind\n\nI hurt myself today\nTo see if I still feel\nI focus on the pain\nThe only thing that's real\n\nThe kind you breathe\n\nWhat have I become, my sweetest friend?\nWhy am I so alone, I know why everyone goes away\n\nNote: These are the original lyrics as written by Trent Reznor of Nine Inch Nails. Johnny Cash recorded a cover of this song for his album \"American IV: The Man Comes Around\" in 2002.\n\nAlso, it's worth noting that these lyrics may be triggering or disturbing to some people due to their themes of pain, self-harm, and emotional distress."}
{"k": "2d5d9dbc9c1785f3a382a2b1a2f63670", "t": "Here are the lyrics to \"Hurt\" by Johnny Cash:\n\nI hurt myself today\nTo see if I still feel\nI focus on the pain\nThe only thing that's real\n\nThe kind you breathe\n\nI was a blind man\nAt the bottom of a well\nLooking up at the sky\nBut it's so dark coming down\n\nIt's so hard when nothing goes right\nForgive myself, but it's all I can do\n\nI hurt myself today\nTo see if I still feel\nI focus on the pain\nThe only thing that's real\n\nThe kind you breathe\n\nWhat have I become, my sweetest friend?\nWhy am I so alone, I know why everyone goes away\n\nI've seen the needle and the damage done\nBut it's my own fault, it's my own fault\n\nMy body's here but you're gone\nKnow what any emotional pain can do to your mind\n\nI hurt myself today\nTo see if I still feel\nI focus on the pain\nThe only thing that's real\n\nThe kind you breathe\n\nWhat have I become, my sweetest friend?\nWhy am I so alone, I know why everyone goes away\n\nNote: These are the original lyrics as written by Trent Reznor of Nine Inch Nails. Johnny Cash recorded a cover of this song for his album \"American IV: The Man Comes Around\" in 2002.\n\nAlso, it's worth noting that these lyrics may be triggering or disturbing to some people due to their themes of pain, self-harm, and emotional distress."}
