{"k": "97ecf2d96adc5b178e63ea9b9a0a3971", "t": "Here's a passage from the novel \"Snow Crash\" by Neal Stephenson:\n\n\"'Listen, I'm gonna tell you something,' said Sanger. 'I've been thinking about this whole thing with Hiro and Y.T. and the Metaverse, and I think I see what's going on here.'\n\n'What is it?' asked Cheese.\n\n'I think we're dealing with a kind of... feedback loop,' said Sanger. 'You know how sometimes you get stuck in a conversation that just goes around in circles? That's what this is like. Hiro and Y.T. are trying to solve the problem, but they're using the same tools that created the problem in the first place.'\n\n'What do you mean?' asked Cheese.\n\n'I mean, think about it,' said Sanger. 'The Metaverse is a virtual reality, right? It's a computer program that simulates a world. But what does that mean, exactly? It means that the people who use it are interacting with a simulation of a world, not the real thing. They're like actors in a play, reciting lines and following a script.'\n\n'And what about Hiro?' asked Cheese.\n\n'Hiro's different,' said Sanger. 'Hiro's a hacker. He's trying to break out of the script, to get beyond the simulation and into the real world. But he's using the same tools that created the problem in the first place - the Metaverse itself.'\n\n'But what about Y.T.?' asked Cheese.\n\n'Y.T.'s different too,' said Sanger. 'She's a delivery girl, not a hacker. She doesn't care about breaking out of the script or getting into the real world. All she cares about is delivering her packages and making some money.'\n\n'So what's going on here?' asked Cheese.\n\n'I think we're seeing a kind of... meta-problem,' said Sanger. 'A problem that exists at multiple levels, simultaneously. The problem in the Metaverse is a reflection of the problem in the real world - it's a feedback loop, like I said before.'\n\n'What do you mean?' asked Cheese.\n\n'I mean, think about it,' said Sanger. 'The Metaverse is a simulation of a world, but what does that say about our own world? Is it just a simulation too?'\n\nCheese looked at him in confusion. 'You're saying the whole world is just a computer program?'\n\nSanger nodded. 'I'm saying that's one possible interpretation. And if that's"}
