{"k": "57e4a95d3efeb50066d1b46d312ed70e", "t": "Here's a passage from \"The Fault in Our Stars\" by John Green:\n\n\"I'm in love with you, Hazel,\" Augustus said, his voice low and serious. \"I'm in love with you, and I know it's crazy and I don't deserve it and I don't expect it to last, but I am.\"\n\nWe were sitting on the edge of the lake, watching the sun set behind the trees. The air was cool and damp, filled with the smell of wet earth and leaves.\n\n\"I'm in love with you too,\" I said, my voice barely above a whisper. \"But that doesn't mean we're going to be okay.\"\n\nAugustus looked at me, his eyes searching mine. \"What do you mean?\"\n\nI shrugged. \"Just that...we're not exactly the poster children for happiness, are we? We're both sick, and we're both going to die young. And even if we weren't sick, we're still just two messed-up teenagers who don't know what they want or where they're going.\"\n\nAugustus nodded thoughtfully. \"Yeah, I guess you're right. But that doesn't mean we can't be happy, Hazel. Or at least...I think it means we can try to be happy, even if it's just for a little while.\"\n\nI looked at him, and he was smiling at me, his eyes crinkling at the corners. And in that moment, I knew that I loved him too, not just because of who he was or what he did, but because of how he made me feel.\n\n\"You're really something, you know that?\" I said, my voice a little stronger now.\n\nAugustus raised an eyebrow. \"What do you mean?\"\n\nI shrugged. \"Just that...you make me feel like maybe we can be okay, even when everything else is falling apart.\"\n\nHe smiled again, and this time it was a big, goofy grin. \"That's the best thing anyone has ever said to me,\" he said.\n\nAnd in that moment, I knew that we were going to be okay, no matter what happened next."}
{"k": "df7bbd021f6eff1964c87ea3656a4b5c", "t": "Here's a passage from \"The Fault in Our Stars\" by John Green:\n\n\"I'm in love with you, Hazel,\" Augustus said, his voice low and serious. \"I'm in love with you, and I know it's crazy and I don't deserve it and I don't expect it to last, but I am.\"\n\nWe were sitting on the edge of the lake, watching the sun set behind the trees. The air was cool and damp, filled with the smell of wet earth and leaves.\n\n\"I'm in love with you too,\" I said, my voice barely above a whisper. \"But that doesn't mean we're going to be okay.\"\n\nAugustus looked at me, his eyes searching mine. \"What do you mean?\"\n\nI shrugged. \"Just that...we're not exactly the poster children for happiness, are we? We're both sick, and we're both going to die young. And even if we weren't sick, we're still just two messed-up teenagers who don't know what they want or where they're going.\"\n\nAugustus nodded thoughtfully. \"Yeah, I guess you're right. But that doesn't mean we can't be happy, Hazel. Or at least...I think it means we can try to be happy, even if it's just for a little while.\"\n\nI looked at him, and he was smiling at me, his eyes crinkling at the corners. And in that moment, I knew that I loved him too, not just because of who he was or what he did, but because of how he made me feel.\n\n\"You're really something, you know that?\" I said, my voice a little stronger now.\n\nAugustus raised an eyebrow. \"What do you mean?\"\n\nI shrugged. \"Just that...you make me feel like maybe we can be okay, even when everything else is falling apart.\"\n\nHe smiled again, and this time it was a big, goofy grin. \"That's the best thing anyone has ever said to me,\" he said.\n\nAnd in that moment, I knew that we were going to be okay, no matter what happened next."}
{"k": "0df9b3f09fe6982f7f1966e8735f28ae", "t": "Here's a passage from \"The Fault in Our Stars\" by John Green:\n\n\"I'm in love with you, Hazel,\" Augustus said, his voice low and serious. \"I'm in love with you, and I know it's crazy and I don't deserve it and I don't expect it to last, but I am.\"\n\nWe were sitting on the edge of the lake, watching the sun set behind the trees. The air was cool and damp, filled with the smell of wet earth and leaves.\n\n\"I'm in love with you too,\" I said, my voice barely above a whisper. \"But that doesn't mean we're going to be okay.\"\n\nAugustus looked at me, his eyes searching mine. \"What do you mean?\"\n\nI shrugged. \"Just that...we're not exactly the poster children for happiness, are we? We're both sick, and we're both going to die young. And even if we weren't sick, we're still just two messed-up teenagers who don't know what they want or where they're going.\"\n\nAugustus nodded thoughtfully. \"Yeah, I guess you're right. But that doesn't mean we can't be happy, Hazel. Or at least...I think it means we can try to be happy, even if it's just for a little while.\"\n\nI looked at him, and he was smiling at me, his eyes crinkling at the corners. And in that moment, I knew that I loved him too, not just because of who he was or what he did, but because of how he made me feel.\n\n\"You're really something, you know that?\" I said, my voice a little stronger now.\n\nAugustus raised an eyebrow. \"What do you mean?\"\n\nI shrugged. \"Just that...you make me feel like maybe we can be okay, even when everything else is falling apart.\"\n\nHe smiled again, and this time it was a big, goofy grin. \"That's the best thing anyone has ever said to me,\" he said.\n\nAnd in that moment, I knew that we were going to be okay, no matter what happened next."}
{"k": "90f8bc1d31e2a75f39e6a51add0c98b0", "t": "Here is a passage from \"The Fault in Our Stars\" by John Green:\n\n\"'I fell in love with you when I was 15 years old,' I said to Hazel, trying to sound casual. 'And I'm not saying that it got any less over time... But the fact is, if I'd fallen in love with you at first sight - and all other things being equal - that changes a person's life forever. You become his world. You never want to leave him, and then you start relying on him for everything except your own happiness.'\n\nHazel raised an eyebrow. 'That sounds like codependency,' she said.\n\n'Codependency is when you're so dependent on someone else that you can't function without them,' I explained. 'But what I'm talking about is different. It's... it's a symbiosis, really. You and the other person are two halves of a whole, and you need each other to be complete.'\n\nHazel looked at me skeptically. 'You're not exactly selling this as a healthy relationship,' she said.\n\nI shrugged. 'Maybe I'm not. But that's just it - it's not about being healthy or unhealthy. It's about being alive. And if you want to know the truth, Hazel, I think we both know what I mean by \"being alive\". We've both been through so much...'\n\nHazel nodded, and for a moment we just sat there in silence, watching the sun set over Amsterdam. 'I'm glad we're doing this,' she said finally.\n\n'What are you talking about?' I asked, but I knew exactly what she meant.\"\n\nThis passage is from Chapter 14 of \"The Fault in Our Stars\", where Hazel and Augustus are discussing their feelings for each other while on a trip to Amsterdam."}
