{"k": "a59622ad902489c9751f3d318d5ae6c5", "t": "Here is a long passage from Chapter 7, \"Mudbloods and Murmurs\", in \"Harry Potter and the Chamber of Secrets\":\n\n\"The Hogwarts Express was moving slowly through the dark countryside now, its carriages swaying gently as it picked up speed. Harry sat in his compartment with Ron and Hermione, trying to make sense of the strange events that had been unfolding since their return to school.\n\n'But why would someone want to open the Chamber again?' Ron asked for what felt like the hundredth time, staring at the ceiling of the compartment as if hoping to find some hidden clue there. 'I mean, it's not just a prank, is it? It's...it's murder.'\n\nHermione shook her head firmly. 'We don't know that yet, Ron. We can't jump to conclusions. But we do know that someone's been using the Chamber, and that they're trying to cover their tracks. I've been thinking about it, and I think I might have a way of finding out who.'\n\nHarry's eyes lit up with interest as he leaned forward in his seat. 'What is it?'\n\nHermione hesitated for a moment before speaking. 'I was talking to Professor Binns yesterday, and he mentioned that the Chamber can only be opened by someone who knows the password. And I think I might have remembered something...'\n\n'What?' Ron and Harry asked together, their voices eager.\n\nHermione's eyes sparkled with excitement as she leaned in closer. 'I remember now! Professor Binns said that the password is always a riddle, and it has to be solved by someone who knows the answer. And I think I might have heard something...'\n\n'What?' Harry asked again, his voice low and urgent.\n\nHermione's face was set in concentration as she tried to remember. 'It was just a whisper, but I'm almost sure of it. Someone said that the password is hidden in an old book...'\n\nRon's eyes widened in understanding. 'The one with the weird symbols on the cover! The one that's always locked away in the restricted section?'\n\nHermione nodded, her face set in determination. 'That's the one. And I think we should try to find out more about it.'\n\nHarry grinned, feeling a surge of excitement at the prospect of solving the mystery. 'Let's do it,' he said, standing up and pulling his bag onto his shoulder.\n\nAs they left the compartment, Ron turned back to Hermione with a mis"}
