\nNotice what has happened here. The wage rate has increased from $12 to $15 per hour, and as a result, the quantity of labor supplied has increased from 20 to 25 hours per week. This is an example of how the supply curve slopes upward: when the wage rate rises, the quantity of labor supplied also increases.\n\nThe supply curve shows that people are willing and able to supply more labor at higher wage rates because they value their leisure"}
