ot knowing exactly where you're going or how you'll get there. Because the truth is, most of us are just winging it anyway. We're all just trying to figure things out as we go along.\n\nAnd that's okay. In fact, it's more than okay - it's liberating. When we accept that we don't have all the answers, and that we can't control everything, then we start to feel a sense of freedom"}
{"k": "a6f7e3d27c292a3a43a5a58a054b83a4", "t": "Here is a passage from \"The Sun and Her Flowers\" by Rupi Kaur:\n\n\"the wound is the place where the light enters you\ni am trying to find the words to describe this feeling\nof being broken open like a flower\npetals unfolding slowly revealing the centre\nwhere the sun shines brightest\n\nit's as if my heart has been ripped from its stem\nand i am left standing here in the dark\ntrying to reattach it but it keeps slipping away\nlike sand between my fingers\n\ni am trying to find the words to describe this feeling\nof being torn apart like a page from a book\nleaving me with nothing but blank space\nwhere stories used to be written\n\nthe wound is the place where the light enters you\nand i am still searching for that light\ntrying to find my way back to the centre\nwhere the sun shines brightest\"\n\nPlease note that this passage is not an exact quote from the book, but rather a generated passage inspired by Rupi Kaur's style and themes."}
