{"k": "5df3c55f000835ba1bcd60ed376d788f", "t": "Here's a generated passage in the style of Rupi Kaur's poetry collection \"Milk and Honey\", which is similar to \"The Sun and Her Flowers\":\n\n**Note:** I'll be generating a passage that follows the typical structure, tone, and language used by Rupi Kaur. However, please keep in mind that this is not an actual poem from her book.\n\n\"your body \nis a map of all the places \nyou've been \nthe scars on your skin \nare the stories you don't tell \neven to yourself \n\nin the mirror \nyou see a stranger's face \none that has been worn down \nby the weight of what you carry \nbut still you hold on \nto the hope that one day \nyou'll be free from the chains \nthat bind you to this earth \n\nyour heart beats for no one \nexcept in your dreams \nwhere love is not a burden \nbut a gentle breeze \nthat rustles through your hair \nand whispers sweet nothings \nin your ear \n\ndo not let anyone \ntell you that you are not enough \nfor they have not seen \nthe beauty of your brokenness \nor the strength of your silence\"\n\nPlease note that this passage is an original creation and not a direct quote from \"The Sun and Her Flowers\" or any other book by Rupi Kaur."}
