sponse to what you're learning from your measurements. This can be hard, especially if you've invested a lot of time and resources into building something that isn't working out as planned. But it's essential for creating a successful startup.\n\nAs I mentioned earlier, the Build-Measure-Learn loop is not just about building products; it's also about building businesses. It's about understanding how customers will use and react to your product, and using that information to inform your decisions about how to grow and scale your business.\n\nIn fact, one of the most important things you can learn from this process is what I"}
