ce.\n\nTheir eyes met for just a moment, and then he was gone, lost in the swirling crowds once more. Celia felt a pang of frustration, but she knew that this was how it would be - a game of cat and mouse, where they chased each other through the circus, always staying one step ahead of the other.\n\nShe smiled to herself as she turned away from the clearing, feeling the thrill of"}
