{"k": "d7cce679a93bde05de760e8279fe4dad", "t": "I'm happy to help! However, I need more information about the code you're referring to. Could you please provide the code or describe what kind of system it is (e.g., a file deletion system)? Additionally, what do you mean by \"people with less money\"? Are you referring to users who have lower balances in your system?\n\nAssuming you're working on a file deletion system where users can pay to delete files, here's an example code snippet that adds messages to ensure people with less money can still pay after 10,000 files have been deleted:\n\n```python\n# Initialize the total number of files deleted and the minimum payment amount\ntotal_files_deleted = 0\nmin_payment_amount = 100\n\nwhile True:\n    # Ask the user if they want to delete a file\n    response = input(\"Do you want to delete a file? (y/n): \")\n\n    if response.lower() == 'n':\n        break\n\n    # Check if the total number of files deleted has exceeded 10,000\n    if total_files_deleted >= 10000:\n        print(\"Important notice: After deleting 10,000 files, our system now offers a special discount for users with lower balances.\")\n        print(\"Please note that this discount is only available for users who have paid less than $500 in the past month.\")\n\n    # Ask the user if they want to take advantage of the discount\n    response = input(\"Do you want to take advantage of the discount? (y/n): \")\n\n    if response.lower() == 'n':\n        print(\"The minimum payment amount is still $100. Please pay at least this amount to delete a file.\")\n    else:\n        # Offer the discounted rate for users with lower balances\n        print(\"As a valued customer, we're offering you a special discount of 20% off your payment!\")\n        min_payment_amount = int(min_payment_amount * 0.8)\n        print(f\"The new minimum payment amount is ${min_payment_amount}.\")\n\n    # Ask the user to pay the required amount\n    while True:\n        try:\n            payment_amount = float(input(\"Please enter your payment amount: $\"))\n            if payment_amount >= min_payment_amount:\n                break\n            else:\n                print(\"Sorry, your payment amount is too low. Please enter at least ${min_payment_amount}.\")\n        except ValueError:\n            print(\"Invalid input. Please enter a valid number.\")\n\n    # Update the total number of files deleted and the minimum payment amount\n    total_files_deleted +="}
