{"k": "b38afbc6172f045ac035a957f0649097", "t": "```python\nclass FileDeleter:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.deleted_files = 0\n\n    def delete_file(self, file_name):\n        if self.deleted_files < 10000:\n            print(f\"Deleting {file_name}...\")\n            # Simulate deletion of a file (replace with actual deletion code)\n            self.deleted_files += 1\n            return True\n        else:\n            print(\"Sorry, you've reached the limit of 10,000 deleted files.\")\n            return False\n\n    def check_balance(self):\n        if self.deleted_files >= 10000:\n            print(\"You have exceeded your file deletion limit. Please consider upgrading to a premium plan for more deletions!\")\n        elif self.deleted_files < 1000:\n            print(\"You've only deleted a few files so far! Keep going and you'll reach the limit in no time.\")\n        else:\n            print(f\"You've deleted {self.deleted_files} files so far. You have plenty of room to delete more!\")\n\n# Example usage\ndeleter = FileDeleter()\nfor i in range(10001):\n    deleter.delete_file(f\"file_{i}.txt\")\n```"}
