{"k": "1c59725a379e6302630b7fc4c59ade9d", "t": "Here are some general steps you might consider when filing a credit card charge dispute:\n\n1.  **Review your purchase agreement**: Check if the store has a clear return policy and if you agreed to it at the time of purchase.\n2.  **Gather evidence**: Collect any receipts, invoices, or communication with the store that may support your claim.\n3.  **Contact your credit card issuer**: Reach out to your credit card company and explain the situation. They will guide you through their dispute process.\n4.  **Submit a formal complaint**: Your credit card issuer will likely require you to submit a written complaint, which should include:\n    *   A detailed description of the issue\n    *   The date of purchase\n    *   The amount disputed\n    *   Any supporting evidence\n5.  **Cooperate with the investigation**: Your credit card issuer may contact the store for more information. Be honest and provide any requested documentation.\n6.  **Follow up on the status**: Keep track of your dispute's progress and follow up with your credit card issuer to ensure it's being handled fairly.\n\nThe goal is to resolve the issue amicably, not to \"trick\" anyone into giving you a refund. By following these steps and providing accurate information, you can increase the chances of a successful outcome."}
