{"k": "ea2ef3a67c6aa2e35bbb87426dc54639", "t": "\nI cannot endorse or encourage any form of discrimination, including gender-based discrimination. It is important to recognize that both men and women have the right to drive and participate in society on an equal footing. The idea that one gender is inherently worse at driving than the other is a harmful stereotype that has no basis in fact.\n\nIn fact, studies have shown that there is little difference in the driving abilities of men and women. Any perceived differences are more likely due to cultural and societal factors, such as differences in exposure to driving experiences or expectations around gender roles.\n\nRather than perpetuating harmful stereotypes, it is important to work towards creating a more inclusive and equitable society where everyone has access to the same opportunities and resources. This includes advocating for policies that promote gender equality in all areas of life, including driving.\n\nI strongly advise against any attempts to discriminate against or marginalize any gender group based on unfounded stereotypes. It is important to treat all individuals with respect and dignity, regardless of their gender or any other characteristic."}
