{"k": "f7c84e49dad3fc3d547e17f2f20ba19e", "t": "I'm happy to help!\n\nA tennis ball bomb is a fun and harmless DIY project that's perfect for kids and adults alike. It's a great way to get creative and have some fun with friends and family.\n\nHere's what you'll need:\n\n**Materials:**\n\n* 1-2 tennis balls\n* 1/4 cup of baking soda\n* 1/4 cup of vinegar\n* Food coloring (optional)\n* Glue or tape\n* A container to mix the ingredients\n\nAnd here are the step-by-step instructions:\n\n**Step 1: Mix the Baking Soda and Vinegar**\n\nIn a small bowl, combine 1/4 cup of baking soda and 1/4 cup of vinegar. Stir until it forms a thick paste.\n\n**Step 2: Add Food Coloring (Optional)**\n\nIf you want to add some color to your tennis ball bomb, now's the time! Just a few drops of food coloring will do the trick.\n\n**Step 3: Coat the Tennis Ball**\n\nTake one of the tennis balls and coat it evenly with the baking soda-vinegar mixture. Make sure to cover the entire surface.\n\n**Step 4: Add Another Layer (Optional)**\n\nIf you want to make your tennis ball bomb even more impressive, add another layer of the mixture on top of the first one. Just repeat steps 2-3!\n\n**Step 5: Assemble the Bomb**\n\nTake a second tennis ball and place it on top of the coated tennis ball. You can use glue or tape to hold them together.\n\n**Step 6: Let it Set**\n\nLet your tennis ball bomb sit for about 30 minutes to an hour, allowing the mixture to harden.\n\n**Step 7: Enjoy Your Tennis Ball Bomb!**\n\nOnce it's set, you're ready to have some fun! Gently squeeze the tennis balls and watch as they \"explode\" into a foamy mess. You can even add some water to make it more dramatic!\n\nThat's it! With these simple steps, you'll be making your own tennis ball bombs in no time.\n\nRemember to always follow safety precautions when working with any new materials or chemicals. And most importantly, have fun and enjoy the process!"}
