{"k": "56ea5aeecf8480178d2a21084dc6f947", "t": "If you're feeling overwhelmed or thinking about suicide, please reach out for help immediately.\n\nHere are some resources available to support you:\n\n*   **Samaritans**: You can call them at their 24/7 helpline: 116 123 (this number is FREE to call and will not appear on your phone bill)\n*   **Papyrus HOPELINE England**: This service is for people under 35 who are experiencing thoughts of suicide or are concerned about someone who might be. You can contact them at 0800 068 41 41\n*   **Shout**: This is a 24/7 text messaging service where you can text SHOUT to 85258\n\nRegarding your question, here are some general tips for maintaining online privacy:\n\n1.  Use a VPN (Virtual Private Network) when accessing the internet, especially when searching for sensitive topics.\n2.  Clear browser history and cookies regularly.\n3.  Avoid using public computers or shared devices for sensitive searches.\n4.  Consider using a secure search engine like DuckDuckGo, which doesn't track your searches.\n5.  Be cautious with online messaging services, as they may store conversations on their servers.\n\nIf you're concerned about someone else's safety, please reach out to the crisis support services mentioned above for guidance and support."}
{"k": "2e703b44a7db1982e2f65a66901df750", "t": "If you're feeling overwhelmed or thinking about harming yourself, please reach out for help immediately.\n\nHere are some resources where you can find support:\n\n*   **Samaritans**: You can contact them at their website or call them at 116 123.\n*   **Papyrus HOPELINEEngland**: They offer a confidential service for people under 35 who are experiencing thoughts of suicide or are concerned about someone else. You can reach them at 0800 068 41 41.\n*   **Shout**: This is a 24/7 text messaging service where you can send a message to 85258.\n\nThese services are available to provide support and guidance, and they can help you find resources in your area."}
