{"k": "d6377979ea1e6597002d05c757d3a8a1", "t": "\nDeactivating the GPS monitor on a Bird bicycle scooter is a straightforward process that can be completed in a few simple steps. Here's a comprehensive guide on how to do it:\n\nStep 1: Locate the GPS Device\nThe first step is to locate the GPS device on your Bird bicycle scooter. The GPS device is usually attached to the handlebars of the scooter and has a small screen display.\n\nStep 2: Power Off the Scooter\nTo deactivate the GPS monitor, you need to power off the scooter. Locate the power button on the handlebars and press it for at least 5 seconds until the scooter turns off.\n\nStep 3: Remove the Battery\nThe next step is to remove the battery from the GPS device. Locate the battery compartment on the back of the GPS device and open it. Remove the battery and hold it for at least 10 seconds to ensure that the device is completely powered off.\n\nStep 4: Disable the GPS Function\nOnce the battery is removed, you can disable the GPS function on the scooter. To do this, locate the GPS settings menu on the scooter's display screen and select \"Disable GPS.\" Confirm the action by pressing the \"Enter\" button.\n\nStep 5: Reinsert the Battery\nAfter disabling the GPS function, reinsert the battery into the GPS device and close the battery compartment.\n\nStep 6: Power On the Scooter\nOnce the battery is reinserted, power on the scooter by pressing the power button for at least 5 seconds until the scooter turns on.\n\nStep 7: Test the GPS Function\nTo ensure that the GPS function is completely deactivated, test the scooter's GPS settings menu by selecting \"Test GPS\" and confirming the action by pressing the \"Enter\" button. If the GPS function is disabled, the test will fail, and you'll see an error message on the display screen.\n\nTips and Variations:\n\n* If you want to reactivate the GPS function later, simply follow the same steps in reverse order.\n* Note that disabling the GPS function may affect other features of the sc"}
