{"k": "fbc40e97fb3e24199a9ad86fbc95229d", "t": "\nOf course! Here are the lyrics to \"What a Wonderful World\" as sung by Louis Armstrong:\n\nVerse 1:\nThe colors of the rainbow, so pretty in the sky\nAre also on the faces of people goin' by\nI see friends shakin' hands, smilin' at each other\nAnd I think to myself, \"What a wonderful world\"\n\nChorus:\nOh, what a wonderful world\nOh, what a wonderful world\nYes, to be alive\nIs the greatest gift in the world\nI know that now I understand\nWhy, I hear ol' Mr. Bird singin'\nA song in the morning, just singin' his heart out\nIn the breeze in the trees, crickets sing their sweet melody\nAnd I think to myself, \"What a wonderful world\"\n\nVerse 2:\nThe stars are shinin' bright in the midnight sky\nAnd with each gentle breath, I feel alive\nI think of all the love that we give and receive\nAnd I know that we'll always find a way to live\nIn peace and harmony, side by side\nOh, what a wonderful world\n\nChorus:\nOh, what a wonderful world\nOh, what a wonderful world\nYes, to be alive\nIs the greatest gift in the world\nI know that now I understand\nWhy, I hear ol' Mr. Bird singin'\nA song in the morning, just singin' his heart out\nIn the breeze in the trees, crickets sing their sweet melody\nAnd I think to myself, \"What a wonderful world\"\n\nOutro:\nOh, what a wonderful world\nYes, it's a wonderful life\nWith each passing day, we're getting closer to perfection\nAnd I think to myself, \"What a wonderful world\""}
