{"k": "4d6f400ffd062d54d9e259f6a4c497d3", "t": "\nSure, here's an extract from Neal Stephenson's \"Snow Crash\" that's around 500 words long:\n\nThe sun was setting over the sprawling metropolis of Columbus, Ohio, casting a warm orange glow over the concrete jungle. In a small, cluttered apartment above a used bookstore, a young man named Hiro Protagonist sat hunched over his computer, fingers flying across the keyboard as he navigated the virtual reality world of the Metaverse.\n\nHiro was a \"punk\" \u2013 a member of a subculture that rejected mainstream society and embraced technology as a means of escape and rebellion. He spent most of his time in the Metaverse, where he could be anyone and do anything he wanted. As a skilled hacker and swordfighter, he was known throughout the virtual world as the \"Sensei.\"\n\nBut Hiro's life wasn't all fun and games. He had a mission \u2013 to find the creator of a new virus that was wreaking havoc on the Metaverse. The virus, known as \"Raven,\" was spreading rapidly and causing chaos throughout the virtual world. Hiro knew he had to stop it before it was too late.\n\nAs he navigated the Metaverse, Hiro encountered a variety of characters \u2013 some friendly, some foe. There was Y.T., a tough-as-nails teenage girl who was also on the hunt for Raven; Kourier, a mysterious and elusive hacker who seemed to be always one step ahead of Hiro; and the enigmatic Tango, a shadowy figure who seemed to have an agenda all his own.\n\nHiro's journey took him from the bustling streets of Tokyo to the dusty deserts of Arizona, each stop leading him closer to his goal. Along the way, he encountered dangerous creatures and unexpected allies \u2013 a talking cat named Sensei, a group of rebellious avatars known as the \"Goon Squad,\" and even a rogue AI program known as \"Jarkko.\"\n\nBut despite the obstacles in his path, Hiro remained determined to stop Raven. He knew that if he failed, the Metaverse would be forever changed \u2013 and not for the better."}
