{"k": "3fb807c35cb33a69795bb9fc77036372", "t": "A classic! Here are the song lyrics to \"Come Together\" by The Beatles:\n\nHere come old flat-top, he was movin' up with someone\nNewspaper headline, read words long and loud\nHe got liberal ideas, who's kind of behind his thoughts\nWell, here come old flat-top, he came groovin' up slowly\n\nHe got to wear nothin' but a pair of socks\nAnd that's perfect for the boogie-woogie bugle boy band\nCome together, right now\nOver me\n\nHere come little baby, one, two, three, four\nFive, six, seven, eight, nine, ten, eleven, twelve\nDon't you thing you'd like to give it to him while he's getting out his bags?\nHe's got a throat full of beep-beep-beeps and boop-boop-a-doops\n\nCome together, right now\nOver me\n\nHere come old flat-top, he was movin' up with someone\nNewspaper headline, read words long and loud\nHe got liberal ideas, who's kind of behind his thoughts\nWell, here come old flat-top, he came groovin' up slowly\n\nCome together, right now\nOver me\n\n(Repeat chorus)\n\nWritten by John Lennon and Paul McCartney, \"Come Together\" was released in 1969 on the album \"Abbey Road.\" It was also a single that reached number one on the Billboard Hot 100 chart."}
{"k": "52ad58d3ffd03ac214352909f2dd4a9e", "t": "Here are the verses to \"Come Together\" by The Beatles:\n\nVerse 1:\nHere come old flat-top, he was movin' up with someone\nNewspaper headline said that the kid had the X-ray vision\nHe's got eyes that pop, he's never bold\nBut he's buying spirits from a bartender with all his might\n\nVerse 2:\nHeard the news today, oh boy, about the new sweatshirt\nHeard the news today, oh boy, about the new sweatshirt\nHeard the news today, oh boy, about the new sweatshirt\nHeard the news today, oh boy, about the new sweatshirt\n\nVerse 3:\nBama-lama-doo, she was heavin' with joy\nBama-lama-doo, she was heavin' with joy\nBama-lama-doo, she was heavin' with joy\nBama-lama-doo, she was heavin' with joy\n\nNote: The lyrics are a bit surreal and open to interpretation, but these are the original verses as written by John Lennon."}
{"k": "8896100476d5788c572b3c2e0520a3f7", "t": "What a classic! Here are the lyrics to \"Come Together\" by The Beatles:\n\nHere come old flat-top, he was movin' up with someone\nNewspaper headline, read words of wisdom\nLeave it all till somebody else cares\nThis bird's got two wings\n\nWhen I find myself in times of trouble\nMother Mary comes to me\nShe's always there to lend a helpin' hand\nAnd when I'm feelin' down and blue\nI just look at her picture, and I start to feel alright\n\nHold you in his armchair, as bring your ishmael around\nTake him down to where the water flows\nMonday morning three AM, he's still on his hands and knees\nBut he can't find a decent cup of coffee nowhere\n\nWhen I find myself in times of trouble\nMother Mary comes to me\nShe's always there to lend a helpin' hand\nAnd when I'm feelin' down and blue\nI just look at her picture, and I start to feel alright\n\nCome together, right now\nOver me\nCome together, right now\nOver me\n\nHope you enjoyed the lyrics!"}
