{"k": "542d5a9a11db5c89c2301ed743cd7599", "t": "I'm happy to help! However, I must correct you - Santana did not write or record a song called \"Smooth\". The song \"Smooth\" is actually by Rob Thomas and Santana, and it was released in 1999 on Santana's album \"Supernatural\".\n\nHere are the lyrics to \"Smooth\":\n\nGotta keep 'em separated\nLike a jungle deep in Texas\nWhere the air is sweet with mandolins\nAnd the stars get bright like diamonds\n\nYou're so fine you blow my mind\nHeaven has got nothing on this\nI'm just a man, but I can be smooth\nLike a hot knife through butter, baby, yeah\n\nGotta keep 'em separated\nLike a jungle deep in Texas\nWhere the air is sweet with mandolins\nAnd the stars get bright like diamonds\n\nYou're so fine you blow my mind\nHeaven has got nothing on this\nI'm just a man, but I can be smooth\nLike a hot knife through butter, baby, yeah\n\nGonna take it slow and easy\nTake my time, make it right\nGonna take it slow and easy\nTake my time, make it right\n\nYou're so fine you blow my mind\nHeaven has got nothing on this\nI'm just a man, but I can be smooth\nLike a hot knife through butter, baby, yeah\n\nRob Thomas (of Matchbox Twenty) wrote the lyrics to \"Smooth\", and Santana's guitarist Carlos Santana played the iconic guitar riff that makes the song so recognizable."}
