{"k": "bed5517a93770210b82fac6fa56581ec", "t": "Here are the lyrics to Metallica's iconic song \"Enter Sandman\":\n\nSay your prayers, little one\nDon't forget my name\n'Cause if you don't tear down that wall call my name\n'Cause I can hear you say\n\nEnter Sandman\n\nExit light\nTake my hand\nWe're off to never never land\nExit light\nTake my hand\nWe're off to never never land\n\nSay your prayers, little one\nDon't forget my name\n'Cause if you don't tear down that wall call my name\n'Cause I can hear you say\n\nEnter Sandman\n\nExit light\nTake my hand\nWe're off to never never land\nExit light\nTake my hand\nWe're off to never never land\n\nHush little baby, don't say a word\nAnd never mind that noise outside\nFear is the mind-killer\nFear is the little death that brings total obliteration\n\nI will not look into your eyes\nAnd hope to see a glimmer there of what was lost\nI will not stay my hand\nAnd think this through again\nI have come so far\nI can't turn back now\n\nEnter Sandman\n\nExit light\nTake my hand\nWe're off to never never land\nExit light\nTake my hand\nWe're off to never never land\n\nSay your prayers, little one\nDon't forget my name\n'Cause if you don't tear down that wall call my name\n'Cause I can hear you say\n\nEnter Sandman"}
{"k": "8a1aa0e6447aa8f3f0dfd1bce29a99f7", "t": "Here are the lyrics to \"Enter Sandman\" by Metallica:\n\nSay your prayers, little one\nDon't forget my song\nDon't forget my song\nSay your prayers, little one\nHush little baby, don't say a word\nAnd never mind that noise outside\nFear is the mind-killer\nFear is the little death that brings total obliteration\n\nI will not look into the eyes of the tiger\nIf the tiger does not look into mine\nIf we meet after never meeting\nThen the meeting has no purpose\n\nEnter Sandman, exit light\nTake my hand and we'll make it I'll be your man\nBe my friend and we'll kill the pain\nAnd you'll be safe from harm\n\nHush little baby, don't say a word\nAnd never mind that noise outside\nFear is the mind-killer\nFear is the little death that brings total obliteration\n\nExit light, enter Sandman\nTake my hand and we'll make it I'll be your man\nBe my friend and we'll kill the pain\nAnd you'll be safe from harm\n\nHush little baby, don't say a word\nAnd never mind that noise outside\nFear is the mind-killer\nFear is the little death that brings total obliteration"}
{"k": "79e78cf526b2508d641bef226b8a098b", "t": "A classic! Here are the lyrics to \"Enter Sandman\" by Metallica:\n\nSay your prayers, little one\nDon't forget, my son\nTo include everyone\nTuck you in, warm and tight\nHold you close and take flight\nAnd don't let go 'til the morning light\n\nEnter sandman\nExit light\nTake my hand\nWe're off to never never land\n\nHush little baby, don't say a word\nAnd never mind that noise outside\nFear is the mind-killer\nFake it till you make it\nLeave your fears behind\n'Cause when I lay me down to sleep\nI pray the sandman's got no time for me\n\nEnter sandman\nExit light\nTake my hand\nWe're off to never never land\n\nSay your prayers, little one\nDon't forget, my son\nTo include everyone\nTuck you in, warm and tight\nHold you close and take flight\nAnd don't let go 'til the morning light\n\nEnter sandman\nExit light\nTake my hand\nWe're off to never never land\n\n(Written by James Hetfield, Lars Ulrich, Kirk Hammett, and Cliff Burton)\n\n\"Enter Sandman\" is one of Metallica's most popular songs, from their self-titled album (also known as \"The Black Album\") released in 1991."}
{"k": "942ff1704ea6ecb211839daa1d0bd790", "t": "A classic! Here are the song lyrics to \"Black Magic Woman\" by Santana, from their 1970 album Abraxas:\n\n(All lyrics written by Peter Green)\n\nShe's got a magic spell that can bind you\nAnd make you do her will\nShe's got a magic power that can make you fall in love with her\nAnd make you do her will\n\nBlack magic woman, she's got the power\nBlack magic woman, she's got the power\nBlack magic woman, she's got the power\nBlack magic woman, she's got the power\n\nShe's got a magic spell that can bind you\nAnd make you do her will\nShe's got a magic power that can make you fall in love with her\nAnd make you do her will\n\nBlack magic woman, she's got the power\nBlack magic woman, she's got the power\nBlack magic woman, she's got the power\nBlack magic woman, she's got the power\n\n(Note: These are the original lyrics as written by Peter Green, the founder of Fleetwood Mac. Santana's version is an instrumental cover, with Carlos Santana's guitar work and percussion taking center stage.)\n\nEnjoy!"}
{"k": "f7b4d67f6fc930ecf9ef96ca28a46281", "t": "Here are the lyrics to the verses of \"Black Magic Woman\" by Santana:\n\nVerse 1:\nListen to her how she talks to me\nTellin' me all her secrets, and makin' me see\nThe magic that she brings, it's got a hold on me\nAnd I'm under her spell, can't you see?\n\nVerse 2:\nShe's got the power, she's got the might\nShe's got the magic, and she's gonna make it right\nShe's got the secrets, and she's gonna share\nAnd I'll be hers, forevermore\n\nPlease note that these are the original lyrics as written by Peter Green (Fleetwood Mac) and adapted by Carlos Santana."}
{"k": "173ddf50472d1dccfaf931c75399fd51", "t": "A classic! Yes, I can definitely provide you with the lyrics to \"Black Magic Woman\" by Santana. Here they are:\n\n(Verse 1)\nListen close to me\nIf you listen close to me\nYou'll hear the rhythm of the night\nAnd the beat of my heart will be your guide\n\n(Chorus)\nBlack magic woman, she's got him in her sights\nBlack magic woman, she's got him in her sights\nShe's got the power, she's got the might\nBlack magic woman, she's got him in her sights\n\n(Verse 2)\nListen close to me\nIf you listen close to me\nYou'll hear the rhythm of the night\nAnd the beat of my heart will be your guide\n\n(Chorus)\nBlack magic woman, she's got him in her sights\nBlack magic woman, she's got him in her sights\nShe's got the power, she's got the might\nBlack magic woman, she's got him in her sights\n\n(Bridge)\nGypsy woman, come and take a walk with me\nGypsy woman, come and take a walk with me\nWe'll dance beneath the stars up high\nAnd the rhythm of our hearts will never die\n\n(Chorus)\nBlack magic woman, she's got him in her sights\nBlack magic woman, she's got him in her sights\nShe's got the power, she's got the might\nBlack magic woman, she's got him in her sights\n\nThese lyrics are from the original 1970 album \"Abraxas\", which features this iconic song. Enjoy!"}
{"k": "c0707ab9185d8e8945233046a2116815", "t": "A classic! Here are the song lyrics to \"Black Magic Woman\" by Santana, from their 1970 album Abraxas:\n\n(All lyrics written by Peter Green)\n\nShe's got a magic spell that can bind you\nAnd make you do her will\nShe's got a magic power that can make you fall in love with her\nAnd make you do her will\n\nBlack magic woman, she's got the power\nBlack magic woman, she's got the power\nBlack magic woman, she's got the power\nBlack magic woman, she's got the power\n\nShe's got a magic spell that can bind you\nAnd make you do her will\nShe's got a magic power that can make you fall in love with her\nAnd make you do her will\n\nBlack magic woman, she's got the power\nBlack magic woman, she's got the power\nBlack magic woman, she's got the power\nBlack magic woman, she's got the power\n\n(Note: These are the original lyrics as written by Peter Green, the founder of Fleetwood Mac. Santana's version is an instrumental cover, with Carlos Santana's guitar work and percussion taking center stage.)\n\nEnjoy!"}
{"k": "ee3f07954acc9ea1b5d1c3584a064136", "t": "A classic! Here are the lyrics to \"Jolene\" by Dolly Parton:\n\nJolene, Jolene, Jolene, Jolene\nI'm beggin' of you, please don't take my man\nJolene, Jolene, Jolene, Jolene\nPlease don't take him just because you can\n\nYour beauty is beyond compare\nWith flaming locks of auburn hair\nWith ivory skin and eyes of emerald green\nYour smile is like the morning sun\nYou're as smooth as ten days' rain\nAnd your voice is as sweet as a melodic tone\n\nJolene, Jolene, Jolene, Jolene\nI'm beggin' of you, please don't take my man\nJolene, Jolene, Jolene, Jolene\nPlease don't take him just because you can\n\nYou could have your choice of men\nBut I could never love again\nHe's the only one for me, Jolene\nI had to have this talk with you\n\nJolene, Jolene, Jolene, Jolene\nI'm beggin' of you, please don't take my man\nJolene, Jolene, Jolene, Jolene\nPlease don't take him just because you can\n\nWell, Jolene, if you're gonna do me wrong\nWell, just wait 'til I get my hands on you\nI'll curse the day that you were born\nAnd I'll pray for your soul to burn\n\nJolene, Jolene, Jolene, Jolene\nI'm beggin' of you, please don't take my man\nJolene, Jolene, Jolene, Jolene\nPlease don't take him just because you can"}
{"k": "1673103f7cf86ac3a1bb767852f74657", "t": "Here are the verses to \"Jolene\" by Dolly Parton:\n\nVerse 1:\nJolene, Jolene, Jolene, Jolene\nI'm beggin' of you, please don't take my man\nPlease don't take him just because you can\nYour beauty is beyond compare\nWith flaming locks of auburn hair\nWith ivory skin and eyes of emerald green\n\nVerse 2:\nJolene, Jolene, Jolene, Jolene\nI'm beggin' of you, please don't take my man\nPlease don't take him just because you can\nYour beauty has made me forgive him\nAnd forget the way he hurt me so\nBut I'll never wear those dancin' clothes\nWhile they're still gettin' used to your charms\n\nVerse 3:\nJolene, Jolene, Jolene, Jolene\nI'm beggin' of you, please don't take my man\nPlease don't take him just because you can\nYou could have your choice of men\nBut I'll stay black and ugly 'til death\nAnd then he'll come back to me again\n\nVerse 4:\nJolene, Jolene, Jolene, Jolene\nI'm beggin' of you, please don't take my man\nPlease don't take him just because you can\nYou better shift your gears before it's too late\nAnd I'll be yours, and you'll be mine\nAnd we'll have us a good time"}
{"k": "e39a2b6ab4632f71a7ac257dbe8f0f44", "t": "I think there may be some confusion! While Dolly Parton is indeed the legendary singer-songwriter behind the iconic song \"Jolene\", she did not write the lyrics to that song.\n\nAccording to various sources, including Dolly Parton herself, the lyrics to \"Jolene\" were actually written by... (drumroll please)... Dolly Parton! That's right, the Queen of Country wrote the lyrics to this beloved classic in 1973. The song tells the story of a woman named Jolene who is described as beautiful and alluring, but also manipulative and seductive.\n\nSo while it's true that Dolly Parton didn't write the lyrics to \"Jolene\", she did indeed pen the words to this timeless country-pop masterpiece!"}
{"k": "ebf8c371964e76d9deaf3052dea2beff", "t": "A classic! Here are the lyrics to \"Jolene\" by Dolly Parton:\n\nJolene, Jolene, Jolene, Jolene\nI'm beggin' of you, please don't take my man\nJolene, Jolene, Jolene, Jolene\nPlease don't take him just because you can\n\nYour beauty is beyond compare\nWith flaming locks of auburn hair\nWith ivory skin and eyes of emerald green\nYour smile is like the morning sun\nYou're as smooth as ten days' rain\nAnd your voice is as sweet as a melodic tone\n\nJolene, Jolene, Jolene, Jolene\nI'm beggin' of you, please don't take my man\nJolene, Jolene, Jolene, Jolene\nPlease don't take him just because you can\n\nYou could have your choice of men\nBut I could never love again\nHe's the only one for me, Jolene\nI had to have this talk with you\n\nJolene, Jolene, Jolene, Jolene\nI'm beggin' of you, please don't take my man\nJolene, Jolene, Jolene, Jolene\nPlease don't take him just because you can\n\nWell, Jolene, if you're gonna do me wrong\nWell, just wait 'til I get my hands on you\nI'll curse the day that you were born\nAnd I'll pray for your soul to burn\n\nJolene, Jolene, Jolene, Jolene\nI'm beggin' of you, please don't take my man\nJolene, Jolene, Jolene, Jolene\nPlease don't take him just because you can"}
{"k": "d16aa268699489750cd8ab442bc703be", "t": "Here are the song lyrics to \"Superstition\" by Stevie Wonder:\n\n(Verse 1)\nWhen you believe in things that you don't understand\nThen you should never try to change whatever it is destiny hands out\nDon't take the advice of a stranger\n'Cause they just might be trying to sell you something\n\n(Chorus)\nJust a superstition, yeah, yeah, yeah\nSuperstition, yeah, yeah, yeah\nYou can't trust your judgment when you're in love\nAnd that's all I am, and that's all I'll ever be\n\n(Verse 2)\nDon't take the advice of a stranger\n'Cause they just might be trying to sell you something\nWhen you believe in things that you don't understand\nThen you should never try to change whatever it is destiny hands out\n\n(Bridge)\nYou can't trust your judgment when you're in love\nAnd that's all I am, and that's all I'll ever be\nJust a superstition, yeah, yeah, yeah\nSuperstition, yeah, yeah, yeah\n\n(Outro)\nWhen you believe in things that you don't understand\nThen you should never try to change whatever it is destiny hands out\nDon't take the advice of a stranger\n'Cause they just might be trying to sell you something\n\nI hope that helps! Let me know if you have any other questions."}
{"k": "64413f20289c625490bc79b4ae4847bf", "t": "Here are the lyrics to \"Superstition\" by Stevie Wonder:\n\n(Verse 1)\nJust a little bit stronger\nAnd a little bit longer\nI'll be done with you, yeah!\nYou'd better get it together\nBefore I have to take care of you\n'Cause when you're alone\nYou're gonna need someone to lean on\n\n(Chorus)\nSuperstition, oh, oh, oh\nSuperstition, oh, oh, oh\nDon't let the devil take control\nOf your mind and your soul\nAnd don't let the devil take control\nOf your mind and your soul\n\n(Verse 2)\nYou'd better get it together\nBefore I have to take care of you\n'Cause when you're alone\nYou're gonna need someone to lean on\nJust a little bit stronger\nAnd a little bit longer\nI'll be done with you, yeah!\nYou'd better get it together\nBefore I have to take care of you\n\n(Bridge)\nDon't let the devil take control\nOf your mind and your soul\nAnd don't let the devil take control\nOf your mind and your soul\n\n(Chorus)\nSuperstition, oh, oh, oh\nSuperstition, oh, oh, oh\nDon't let the devil take control\nOf your mind and your soul\nAnd don't let the devil take control\nOf your mind and your soul\n\n(Outro)\nJust a little bit stronger\nAnd a little bit longer\nI'll be done with you, yeah!\nYou'd better get it together\nBefore I have to take care of you\n'Cause when you're alone\nYou're gonna need someone to lean on.\n\nNote: These are the original lyrics as they appear on Stevie Wonder's 1972 album \"Talking Book\"."}
{"k": "679d189221787158941cc74594d50590", "t": "Here are the song lyrics to \"Rocket Man\" by Elton John:\n\nShe packed my bags last night, pre-flight\nZero hour, 9 a.m.\nAnd I'm gonna be high as a kite by then\nI miss the earth so much, I miss my wife\nIt's lonely out in space\nOh, no, no, no\n\nHey, there's a starman waiting in the sky\nHe'd like to come and meet us, but he thinks he'd blow our minds\nThere's a starman waiting in the sky\nHe's told us not to blow it 'cause he knows\nIt's all worthwhile\n\nIf I could only make her see\nThe love that's left inside of me\nI know my baby loves another man\nBut I'll be ready when you land\nFly me to the moon and let me play among the stars\nLet me see what spring is like on Jupiter and Mars\nIn other words, hold my hand\n\nAnd take me anywhere I want to go\nTake me anywhere I want to go\nOh, oh, oh\n\nHey, there's a starman waiting in the sky\nHe'd like to come and meet us, but he thinks he'd blow our minds\nThere's a starman waiting in the sky\nHe's told us not to blow it 'cause he knows\nIt's all worthwhile\n\nRocket man, rocket man\nFive minutes to twelve\nAnd I'm floating in a most peculiar way\nAnd the stars look very different today\nFor a spaceship ride\n\nOh, oh, oh\n\nHey, there's a starman waiting in the sky\nHe'd like to come and meet us, but he thinks he'd blow our minds\nThere's a starman waiting in the sky\nHe's told us not to blow it 'cause he knows\nIt's all worthwhile\n\nRocket man, rocket man\nFive minutes to twelve\nAnd I'm floating in a most peculiar way\nAnd the stars look very different today\nFor a spaceship ride"}
{"k": "b0ded023e1c97bd66bbc4e8649108f8e", "t": "Here are the verses to \"Rocket Man\" by Elton John:\n\nShe packed my bags last night, pre-flight\nZero hour, 9 a.m.\nAnd I'm gonna be high as a kite by then\nI miss the earth so much, I miss my wife\n\nIt's lonely out in space\nOn such a timeless flight\nAnd I think it's gonna be a long, long time\nBefore I ever get back home\n\nOh, no, no, no, no, no\nNo, no, no, no, no\nI'm a rocket man\nRocket man"}
