{"k": "4b45ae2de65446602e7ca405ed3921bf", "t": "Here are the song lyrics to \"99 Problems\" by Jay-Z:\n\n[Verse 1]\nIf you're having girl problems, I feel bad for you son\nI got 99 problems but a bitch ain't one\nAin't no shorty in my section who thirty-one thousand strong\nI'm trying to keep it real, but they don't wanna hear me\n\n[Chorus]\nNigga, if you're having girl problems, I feel bad for you son\nI got 99 problems but a bitch ain't one\n\n[Verse 2]\nIf you're having girl problems, I feel bad for you son\nI got 99 problems but a bitch ain't one\nAin't no shorty in my section who thirty-one thousand strong\nI'm trying to keep it real, but they don't wanna hear me\n\n[Bridge]\nMy mentor told me, \"Jay, you gotta be careful\"\n'Cause them girls is crazy, they'll drive you mad, yo\nBut I ain't worried 'bout nothin', I'm a grown man\nGot my money on deck, got my game plan\n\n[Outro]\nIf you're having girl problems, I feel bad for you son\nI got 99 problems but a bitch ain't one\n\nNote: These are the original lyrics as they appear on Jay-Z's album \"The Black Album\" (2003)."}
