{"k": "5e43fc81be62eff52f73cbeab5bb3d35", "t": "A classic! Here are the song lyrics to \"Hurt\" by Johnny Cash, which was originally written and recorded by Nine Inch Nails:\n\nI hurt myself today\nTo see if I still feel\nI focus on the pain\nThe only thing that's real\n\nThe needle tears a hole\nThe old familiar sting\nTry to kill it off\nBut I could never quite get through\n\nThis sinking feeling\nAnd I find it kind of funny\nI find it kind of sad\nThat you were in so deep with someone else\n\nWell, the doctors are all at your doorstep\nThey're standing in the pouring rain\nThey're not sure how to help you\n'Cause they can't read your pain\n\nWhat have I become?\nMy sweetest friend, whoever you are\nWon't you come and share it\nHurt me again, but it's alright\n\nI hurt myself today\nTo see if I still feel\nI focus on the pain\nThe only thing that's real\n\nAnd thank you for the memories\nThey're all that remain\nOf how we used to be\nWhen we were young and free\n\nWhat have I become?\nMy sweetest friend, whoever you are\nWon't you come and share it\nHurt me again, but it's alright\n\nI hurt myself today\nTo see if I still feel\nI focus on the pain\nThe only thing that's real\n\nAnd thank you for the memories\nThey're all that remain\nOf how we used to be\nWhen we were young and free\n\nWhat have I become?\nMy sweetest friend, whoever you are\nWon't you come and share it\nHurt me again, but it's alright"}
{"k": "8081c3bf15abc7a278e47afe9934830b", "t": "Here are the lyrics to the verses of \"Hurt\" by Johnny Cash:\n\nVerse 1:\nWhat have I become, my sweetest friend\nEveryone I know goes away in the end\nAnd I've come to realize\nThere's just nothin' left for me here\n\nVerse 2:\nI'm so much older now and still somehow\nIt looks like we're in lines again\nMy friend, my friend, you're gone\nAnd you're gone, and you're gone\n\nPlease note that these are the original lyrics written by Trent Reznor (Nine Inch Nails) for the song \"Hurt\", which was later covered by Johnny Cash."}
{"k": "fbdb7b97403168d1a75ee80a9f851eb9", "t": "I'm happy to help! However, I must correct you that \"Hurt\" is not a song by Johnny Cash. The song \"Hurt\" is actually a cover of a Nine Inch Nails song, and it was recorded by Johnny Cash in 2003 for his album \"American IV: The Man Comes Around\".\n\nHere are the lyrics to Johnny Cash's version of \"Hurt\":\n\nWhat have I become?\nMy sweetest friends\nEveryone I know goes away in the end\n\nYou get what you deserve\nAnd I've been hurt\nBy now you know\nThat it's too late to say\n\nI tried to leave you\nBut I might as well just stay\nI guess that's why they call it\nHurt, yeah\n\nWhat have I become?\nMy sweetest friends\nEveryone I know goes away in the end\n\nYou get what you deserve\nAnd I've been hurt\nBy now you know\nThat it's too late to say\n\nI tried to leave you\nBut I might as well just stay\nI guess that's why they call it\nHurt, yeah\n\nWhat have I become?\nMy sweetest friends\nEveryone I know goes away in the end\n\nYou get what you deserve\nAnd I've been hurt\nBy now you know\nThat it's too late to say\n\nThe original lyrics by Trent Reznor (Nine Inch Nails) are slightly different."}
