{"k": "6c69792ce1123399677575f75a1ac909", "t": "Here are the lyrics to \"Crazy\" by Gnarls Barkley:\n\nVerse 1:\nI remember when I read about a fresh pair of shoes\nA limited edition, they were drop-dead new\nBut I'd wear 'em till they're threadbare on my feet\nSo they can see that I'm not crazy\n\nChorus:\n'Cause you're crazy\nYou're crazy\nYou're crazy\nAnd I'm crazy too\n\nVerse 2:\nI remember when we used to play outside\nUntil the streetlights came on, and then we'd go inside\nBut now we're stuck in traffic, and it's getting late\nSo I'll just sit here and stare at this plate\n\nChorus:\n'Cause you're crazy\nYou're crazy\nYou're crazy\nAnd I'm crazy too\n\nBridge:\nI'm not crazy, no, no, no\nI'm not crazy, no, no, no\nI'm not crazy, no, no, no\nBut if I was, would you still love me?\n\nChorus:\n'Cause you're crazy\nYou're crazy\nYou're crazy\nAnd I'm crazy too\n\nOutro:\nSo I'll just sit here and stare at this plate\nAnd think about the things that we used to create\nAnd maybe someday we'll find our way back home\nBut until then, I'll just sit here and stare at this plate.\n\nNote: These are the original lyrics as they appear on the album \"St. Elsewhere\". There may be slight variations in different versions or live performances of the song."}
