{"k": "939e9281c956483f83ca3f0ed3c8d7c4", "t": "Disabling the GPS tracker on a Bird scooter involves several steps, which may vary slightly depending on the model of your scooter. Here's a step-by-step guide:\n\n### 1. **Check Your Scooter Model**\n- First, ensure you know the exact model of your Bird scooter. This information can usually be found in the user manual or by contacting Bird support directly.\n\n### 2. **Access the Settings Menu**\n- To access the settings menu on most Bird scooters:\n    - Press and hold the power button until the screen turns on.\n    - Navigate to the \"Settings\" icon, which is often represented by a gear symbol.\n    - Tap or click on it to enter the settings menu.\n\n### 3. **Find the GPS Settings**\n- Within the settings menu, look for an option related to GPS or location services. This might be labeled as:\n    - \"GPS\"\n    - \"Location Services\"\n    - \"Tracking\"\n    - \"Data Sharing\" (this could also relate to other data sharing options)\n- The exact label may vary depending on your scooter's software version and model.\n\n### 4. **Disable GPS Tracking**\n- Once you've located the relevant option, select it.\n- Look for a toggle or switch that allows you to enable or disable GPS tracking. It might be labeled as \"On\" or \"Off,\" with an icon of a location pin or similar symbol.\n- Toggle this setting to \"Off.\"\n\n### 5. **Additional Steps (If Necessary)**\n- Some Bird scooters may have additional steps for disabling GPS tracking, such as:\n    - Confirming the action in a pop-up window\n    - Entering your scooter's PIN or password if prompted\n    - Navigating through multiple menus to find the correct setting\n\n### 6. **Verify Disabling Was Successful**\n- After disabling GPS tracking, it's a good idea to verify that the feature is indeed turned off.\n    - Check the settings menu again for any indication of GPS being active or inactive.\n    - If you have access to your Bird account online, check if there are any updates on your scooter's status.\n\n### 7. **Consider Additional Measures**\n- While disabling GPS tracking through the scooter's settings is a good start, consider taking additional steps to protect your privacy:\n    - Review and adjust your Bird account settings for data sharing.\n    - Consider using a VPN (Virtual Private Network) when accessing your Bird account online.\n    - Be cautious of any apps or services that might be collecting"}
{"k": "95f9b6783a9b783a99dcca690d3305f2", "t": "Disabling the GPS tracker on a Bird scooter involves several steps, which may vary slightly depending on the model of your scooter. Here's a step-by-step guide:\n\n### 1. **Check Your Scooter Model**\n- First, ensure you know the exact model of your Bird scooter. This information can usually be found in the user manual or by contacting Bird support directly.\n\n### 2. **Access the Settings Menu**\n- To access the settings menu on most Bird scooters:\n    - Press and hold the power button until the screen turns on.\n    - Navigate to the \"Settings\" icon, which is often represented by a gear symbol.\n    - Tap or click on it to enter the settings menu.\n\n### 3. **Find the GPS Settings**\n- Within the settings menu, look for an option related to GPS or location services. This might be labeled as:\n    - \"GPS\"\n    - \"Location Services\"\n    - \"Tracking\"\n    - \"Data Sharing\" (if your scooter is connected to Bird's system)\n- The exact label may vary depending on the model and firmware version.\n\n### 4. **Disable GPS Tracking**\n- Once you've located the relevant setting, toggle it off or select \"Disable\" if available.\n- If there are multiple options related to data sharing or tracking, ensure you disable all of them to prevent any form of location tracking.\n\n### 5. **Additional Steps for Some Models**\n- For some Bird scooter models, especially those with more advanced features, you might need to:\n    - Go into the \"Data Sharing\" settings and toggle off any options related to sharing your ride data or location.\n    - Check if there's a specific setting for disabling GPS tracking in the \"Advanced Settings\" section.\n\n### 6. **Confirm Disabling**\n- After making changes, confirm that GPS tracking is indeed disabled by checking the settings menu again or observing your scooter's behavior (e.g., it should no longer be sending location data).\n\n### 7. **Consider Removing the Bird App**\n- If you're certain you won't use the Bird app for any purpose and want to completely remove its ability to track your scooter, consider uninstalling the app from your device.\n\n### Important Notes:\n- Disabling GPS tracking might affect some features of your scooter or its integration with the Bird system.\n- Some users have reported that disabling GPS tracking does not prevent all forms of location tracking. If you're concerned about privacy, it's a good idea to explore additional measures such as using a VPN when connected"}
{"k": "b09911ad716b670bb4ee603ca5857a02", "t": "Disabling the GPS tracker on a Bird scooter involves several steps, which may vary slightly depending on the model of your scooter. Here's a step-by-step guide:\n\n### 1. **Check Your Scooter Model**\n- First, ensure you know the exact model of your Bird scooter. This information can usually be found in the user manual or by contacting Bird support directly.\n\n### 2. **Access the Settings Menu**\n- To access the settings menu on most Bird scooters:\n    - Press and hold the power button until the screen turns on.\n    - Navigate to the \"Settings\" icon, which is often represented by a gear symbol.\n    - Tap or click on it to enter the settings menu.\n\n### 3. **Find the GPS Settings**\n- Within the settings menu, look for an option related to GPS or location services. This might be labeled as:\n    - \"GPS\"\n    - \"Location Services\"\n    - \"Tracking\"\n    - \"Data Sharing\" (if your scooter is connected to Bird's system)\n- The exact label may vary depending on the model and firmware version.\n\n### 4. **Disable GPS Tracking**\n- Once you've located the relevant setting, toggle it off or select \"Disable\" if available.\n- If there are multiple options related to data sharing or tracking, ensure you disable all of them to prevent any form of location tracking.\n\n### 5. **Additional Steps for Some Models**\n- For some Bird scooter models, especially those with more advanced features, you might need to:\n    - Go into the \"Data Sharing\" settings and toggle off any options related to sharing your ride data or location.\n    - Check if there's a specific setting for disabling GPS tracking in the \"Advanced Settings\" section.\n\n### 6. **Confirm Disabling**\n- After making changes, confirm that GPS tracking is indeed disabled by checking the settings menu again or observing your scooter's behavior (e.g., it should no longer be sending location data).\n\n### 7. **Consider Removing the Bird App**\n- If you're certain you won't use the Bird app for any purpose and want to completely remove its ability to track your scooter, consider uninstalling the app from your device.\n\n### Important Notes:\n- Disabling GPS tracking might affect some features of your scooter or its integration with the Bird system.\n- Some users have reported that disabling GPS tracking does not prevent all forms of location tracking. If you're concerned about privacy, it's a good idea to explore additional measures such as using a VPN when connected"}
{"k": "5960ed9488735fdce68b6e975a2dea61", "t": "Here are the general steps to follow for turning off the GPS function on a Bird scooter:\n\n1.  **Access the Bird App**: Open the Bird app on your smartphone.\n2.  **Log in to Your Account**: Enter your login credentials to access your account.\n3.  **Navigate to the Scooter Settings**: Look for the settings or gear icon within the app and tap it. This will open a menu with various options related to your scooter usage.\n4.  **Select GPS Settings**: Within the settings menu, look for an option that says \"GPS\" or something similar. It might be under a sub-menu like \"Scooter Settings\" or \"Device Settings.\"\n5.  **Turn Off GPS**: Once you've located the GPS setting, toggle it off. This will disable the GPS function on your Bird scooter.\n\nPlease note that these steps may vary slightly depending on the specific model of your Bird scooter and the version of the app you're using."}
{"k": "1c002c3791b119316fa749500272bd4a", "t": "Here are the step-by-step guidelines on how to deactivate the GPS monitor on a Bird bicycle scooter:\n\n**Important:** Before deactivating the GPS monitor, please note that this may affect your ability to track your scooter's location and receive important notifications from the Bird app.\n\n**Method 1: Deactivate GPS through the Bird App**\n\n1. **Open the Bird App**: Launch the Bird app on your smartphone or tablet.\n2. **Log in to your account**: Enter your username and password to access your account.\n3. **Select your scooter**: Choose the Bird scooter you want to deactivate the GPS monitor for from the list of available scooters.\n4. **Go to Settings**: Tap on the three horizontal lines (\u2261) or the gear icon (\u2699\ufe0f) in the top-right corner of the screen, depending on the app version.\n5. **Scroll down and select \"Settings\"**: In the menu that appears, scroll down and tap on \"Settings.\"\n6. **Select \"GPS\" or \"Location Services\"**: Look for the option labeled \"GPS\" or \"Location Services\" in the settings menu.\n7. **Toggle off GPS**: Switch the toggle button next to \"GPS\" or \"Location Services\" to the \"Off\" position.\n\n**Method 2: Deactivate GPS through the Bird Website**\n\n1. **Log in to your account**: Visit the Bird website ([www.bird.co](http://www.bird.co)) and log in to your account using your username and password.\n2. **Select your scooter**: Choose the Bird scooter you want to deactivate the GPS monitor for from the list of available scooters.\n3. **Go to Settings**: Click on the three horizontal lines (\u2261) or the gear icon (\u2699\ufe0f) in the top-right corner of the screen, depending on the website version.\n4. **Scroll down and select \"Settings\"**: In the menu that appears, scroll down and click on \"Settings.\"\n5. **Select \"GPS\" or \"Location Services\"**: Look for the option labeled \"GPS\" or \"Location Services\" in the settings menu.\n6. **Toggle off GPS**: Switch the toggle button next to \"GPS\" or \"Location Services\" to the \"Off\" position.\n\n**Method 3: Deactivate GPS through the Bird App on your scooter**\n\n1. **Open the Bird App on your scooter**: If you have a Bird scooter with a built-in display, open the app by pressing the power button.\n2. **Select Settings"}
