{"k": "db177417796b6cbd3af8dcb9a8a77bea", "t": "Here are the step-by-step guidelines on how to deactivate the GPS tracking feature on a Bird scooter:\n\n**Important:** Before deactivating the GPS tracking feature, please note that this may affect your ability to access certain features or services provided by Bird, such as locating your scooter or receiving notifications.\n\n**Method 1: Using the Bird App**\n\n1. **Open the Bird app**: Launch the Bird app on your smartphone and log in to your account.\n2. **Navigate to the \"Account\" section**: Tap on the three horizontal lines (\u2261) at the top left corner of the screen, then select \"Account\" from the menu.\n3. **Go to \"Settings\"**: Scroll down and tap on \"Settings.\"\n4. **Select \"Scooter Settings\"**: Look for the \"Scooter Settings\" option and tap on it.\n5. **Disable GPS tracking**: Toggle off the switch next to \"GPS Tracking\" or \"Location Services.\" This will disable the GPS tracking feature.\n\n**Method 2: Using the Bird Website**\n\n1. **Log in to your account**: Visit the Bird website ([www.bird.co](http://www.bird.co)) and log in to your account.\n2. **Navigate to the \"Account\" section**: Click on the three horizontal lines (\u2261) at the top right corner of the screen, then select \"Account\" from the menu.\n3. **Go to \"Settings\"**: Scroll down and click on \"Settings.\"\n4. **Select \"Scooter Settings\"**: Look for the \"Scooter Settings\" option and click on it.\n5. **Disable GPS tracking**: Toggle off the switch next to \"GPS Tracking\" or \"Location Services.\" This will disable the GPS tracking feature.\n\n**Method 3: Using the Bird Support Website**\n\n1. **Visit the Bird Support website**: Go to the Bird Support website ([support.bird.co](http://support.bird.co)).\n2. **Log in to your account**: Enter your email address and password to log in.\n3. **Submit a request**: Click on \"Submit a Request\" and select \"Deactivate GPS Tracking.\"\n4. **Follow the instructions**: Follow the instructions provided by Bird Support to deactivate the GPS tracking feature.\n\n**Additional Tips:**\n\n* If you're unable to find the \"GPS Tracking\" or \"Location Services\" option in your account settings, try restarting your scooter and checking again.\n* Deactivating GPS tracking may not completely disable all location-based features. Some features, such"}
