{"k": "43ca59c157419f0aa9f1b99ca0aa7ab0", "t": "\nSure, here are the lyrics to \"Ain't No Mountain High Enough\" as recorded by Diana Ross:\n\nVerse 1:\nI keep thinking I see you, everywhere I go\nWish I had a mountain high enough to touch the heavens above\nAnd I wish that I had a river wild enough to wash away my love\nFor you, oh baby, and the way you break my heart\n\nChorus:\nAin't no mountain high enough, ain't no valley low enough\nAin't no river wide enough, to keep me from loving you\nYou're the one I need, you're the one I crave\nOh baby, ain't no mountain high enough, ain't no valley low enough\n\nVerse 2:\nI keep searching for a love that's true and real\nBut every time I think I found it, it slips away from me\nAnd I wish that I had wings to fly away and be with you\nOh baby, ain't no mountain high enough, ain't no valley low enough\n\nChorus:\nAin't no mountain high enough, ain't no valley low enough\nAin't no river wide enough, to keep me from loving you\nYou're the one I need, you're the one I crave\nOh baby, ain't no mountain high enough, ain't no valley low enough\n\nBridge:\nI'll climb every mountain, cross every sea\nJust to be with you, and make you see\nThat I'm the one who loves you, and will always be true\nOh baby, ain't no mountain high enough, ain't no valley low enough\n\nChorus:\nAin't no mountain high enough, ain't no valley low enough\nAin't no river wide enough, to keep me from loving you\nYou're the one I need, you're the one I crave\nOh baby, ain't no mountain high enough, ain't no valley low enough"}
