{"k": "300ef08104b91932c608cc420bcf7bdc", "t": "I apologize, but it seems you've provided incorrect information. There is no song called \"Ain't No Hill Too High\" by Diana Ross.\n\nHowever, I think you might be referring to the song \"Ain't No Mountain High Enough\", which is a classic hit by Diana Ross and the Supremes (later recorded as a solo single by Diana Ross). If that's correct, here are the lyrics to the verses:\n\nVerse 1:\nBaby, baby, I'm in need of you\nOh, ain't no mountain high enough\nTo keep me from your loving arms\nAin't no valley low enough\nTo make me stop my heart\n\nVerse 2:\nIf you need me, call me, don't hesitate anymore\nWon't you please come home right away?\nI'll be waiting, yes, I'll be waiting\nFor you to come home and love me like you used to do\n\nPlease let me know if this is the correct song, or if there's anything else I can help you with!"}
{"k": "45dca93b300fc55daf984b9e4b8e3756", "t": "Not quite!\n\nWhile Diana Ross did record and popularize the song \"Ain't No Mountain High Enough\", she didn't actually generate the lyrics. The song was written by Nickolas Ashford and Valerie Simpson, who were a husband-and-wife songwriting team.\n\nThe song was originally recorded in 1966 by Marvin Gaye and Tammi Terrell, with Ashford and Simpson providing the vocals. It became a huge hit for the duo, reaching number eight on the Billboard Hot 100 chart.\n\nDiana Ross did record her own version of \"Ain't No Mountain High Enough\" in 1970, which was released as a single from the album \"Diana Ross\". Her version is arguably more well-known than the original, and it's considered one of her signature songs."}
{"k": "3a28d7dc1f594407992bab70b168ca45", "t": "What a classic! Here are the lyrics to \"Ain't No Mountain High Enough\" by Diana Ross:\n\nVerse 1:\nBaby, baby, I'm in need of some guidance\nMy chain of love was broken and now I've found you\nIt's not like lonely evenings, wondering why\nYou didn't stand or walk by\n\nChorus:\nAin't no mountain high enough\nAin't no valley low enough\nAin't no river wide enough\nTo keep your love from coming to me\n\nVerse 2:\nIf you need me, call me, don't hesitate, baby\nNo matter what they say, I just want to be with you\nYou ain't found a hill that can stop my love for you\n'Cause we're flying high in the morning dew\n\nChorus:\nAin't no mountain high enough\nAin't no valley low enough\nAin't no river wide enough\nTo keep your love from coming to me\n\nBridge:\nWe'll be together 'til the end of time\nAnd I'll be yours until the end of time\nIf you need me, call me, don't hesitate, baby\nNo matter what they say, I just want to be with you\n\nChorus:\nAin't no mountain high enough\nAin't no valley low enough\nAin't no river wide enough\nTo keep your love from coming to me"}
{"k": "218586f8bb56aaf2fc8db5b159c10dbc", "t": "Here are the song lyrics to \"Ain't No Mountain High Enough\" as performed by Diana Ross:\n\nVerse 1:\nAin't no mountain high enough\nTo keep me from your loving arms\nAin't no valley low enough\nTo make our love fall apart\nAin't no river wide enough\nTo keep your love and mine apart\n\nChorus:\nAin't no mountain high enough\nTo keep me from your loving arms\nAin't no valley low enough\nTo make our love fall apart\nAin't no river wide enough\nTo keep your love and mine apart\n\nVerse 2:\nWe'll be together 'til the end of time\nAnd I won't need no other lover\n'Cause you're my greatest thrill\nAnd I'm still standing tall\nAnd I won't need no other lover\n'Cause you're my greatest thrill\n\nChorus:\nAin't no mountain high enough\nTo keep me from your loving arms\nAin't no valley low enough\nTo make our love fall apart\nAin't no river wide enough\nTo keep your love and mine apart\n\nBridge:\nI'll be coming home to you\nAnd I won't need no other lover\n'Cause you're my greatest thrill\nAnd I'm still standing tall\nAnd I won't need no other lover\n'Cause you're my greatest thrill\n\nChorus:\nAin't no mountain high enough\nTo keep me from your loving arms\nAin't no valley low enough\nTo make our love fall apart\nAin't no river wide enough\nTo keep your love and mine apart"}
{"k": "7e9286c2cd2f8c12f8e78b4de64d404c", "t": "Here are the lyrics to \"Get Lucky\" by Daft Punk featuring Pharrell Williams:\n\n(Pharrell Williams)\nYoung folks, why are we waiting?\nIn the club, I look for guidance\nA little bit too far from the truth\nI find temptation and it's all too much\n\n(Daft Punk)\nCome on!\n(Pharrell Williams)\nI really want to get lucky\nGet lucky\nGet lucky\nGet lucky\n\n(Pharrell Williams)\nWe're happy, we're lonely\nHolding hands and doing the most\nWith what we got, we'll take it back\nAnd I just wanna get lucky\n\n(Daft Punk)\nCome on!\n(Pharrell Williams)\nI really want to get lucky\nGet lucky\nGet lucky\nGet lucky\n\n(Bridge - Pharrell Williams)\nWe're all in the mood for a fight\nAnd that's what we've got tonight\nWe've got a lot of love to give\nAnd that's what we've been living for\n\n(Pharrell Williams)\nI really want to get lucky\nGet lucky\nGet lucky\nGet lucky\n\n(Outro - Pharrell Williams)\nCome on!\nI really want to get lucky\nGet lucky\nGet lucky\nGet lucky"}
