{"k": "19066a43efcb07f661348204d07f5392", "t": "Here are the lyrics to \"Get Lucky\" by Daft Punk featuring Pharrell Williams:\n\n(Pharrell Williams)\nYoung folks, why are we waiting?\nIn the club, we just wanna party\nWe're happy, don't you know it?\n'Cause I got that...\n\n(Daft Punk)\nGet lucky\nGet lucky\n\n(Pharrell Williams)\nCome on, come on, come on\nLet's get lucky\nCome on, come on, come on\nLet's get lucky\n\n(Pharrell Williams)\nWe've come too far\nTo give up now\nStart pumping the big bass\nGive me some space for your hips\n\n(Daft Punk)\nGet lucky\nGet lucky\n\n(Pharrell Williams)\nDon't stop, don't stop, don't stop\nGetting lucky\nDon't stop, don't stop, don't stop\nGetting lucky\n\n(Daft Punk)\nGet lucky\nGet lucky\n\n(Pharrell Williams)\nWe're happy, don't you know it?\n'Cause I got that...\n\n(Daft Punk)\nGet lucky\nGet lucky\n\nNote: These are the main lyrics to the song. There may be some additional vocals or sound effects throughout the track that aren't included here."}
{"k": "4c36648b0c2241d580777bb8e4349567", "t": "That's not entirely accurate. While Pharrell Williams did collaborate with Daft Punk on their hit single \"Get Lucky\", he was not a featured artist in the classical sense.\n\nAccording to various sources, including interviews with Pharrell himself, his role in the song was more akin to a co-writer and vocalist. He contributed lyrics and vocals to the track, which was written by Guy-Manuel de Homem-Christo and Thomas Bangalter of Daft Punk, along with Pharrell.\n\nIn other words, Pharrell's voice is prominent on the song, but he is not credited as a featured artist in the same way that a guest rapper or singer might be. Instead, his contributions are more integrated into the fabric of the song, which is characteristic of Daft Punk's collaborative approach to music-making."}
{"k": "9fdd3b13927b4841910db6cf9de64422", "t": "Here are the song lyrics to \"Get Lucky\" by Daft Punk, featuring Pharrell Williams:\n\n[Pharrell Williams]\nYoung folks, why are we waiting?\nIn the club, we just wanna party\nWe're happy, don't you know it?\n\n[Chorus]\nGet lucky, get lucky\nGet lucky, get lucky\n\n[Pharrell Williams]\nCome on, come on, come on, come on\nAnd put this record on\nI was lost and now I'm found\n'Cause you got that magic, where do we begin?\nThe present has no ribbon\nOn your problems, my friend\nTook a good hard look at it\nAnd it's all okay\n\n[Chorus]\nGet lucky, get lucky\nGet lucky, get lucky\n\n[Pharrell Williams]\nWe've come too far\nTo give up this cloud nine\nYou're happy, I'm drunk\nSo let's go all night\n'Cause we got that magic\nWhere do we begin?\nThe present has no ribbon\nOn your problems, my friend\nTook a good hard look at it\nAnd it's all okay\n\n[Chorus]\nGet lucky, get lucky\nGet lucky, get lucky\n\n[Bridge]\nWe're happy, don't you know it?\n\n[Pharrell Williams]\nCome on, come on, come on, come on\nAnd put this record on\nI was lost and now I'm found\n'Cause you got that magic, where do we begin?\nThe present has no ribbon\nOn your problems, my friend\nTook a good hard look at it\nAnd it's all okay\n\n[Chorus]\nGet lucky, get lucky\nGet lucky, get lucky"}
{"k": "61e5ef88c9331b16620245b3845c4a13", "t": "Here are the lyrics to \"Bad Guy\" by Billie Eilish:\n\nYou like that, don't you?\nDon't you, don't you, don't you?\n\nI'm a bad guy\nI'm a bad guy\nI'm a bad guy\nI'm a bad guy\n\nYou're a good girl\nCan't be bought\nAll of the boys think she's a toy\nJust because she wears nothin' but her sauce\n\nAnd if she brings her West Coast friends, they'll be like \"Oh, what a night\"\nBut we'll be smokin' in the boys' club 'til we run out of time\nSo she plays it cool, but I can see through\nShe's just a bad guy, yeah, yeah, yeah\n\nYou like that, don't you?\nDon't you, don't you, don't you?\n\nI'm a bad guy\nI'm a bad guy\nI'm a bad guy\nI'm a bad guy\n\nYou're a good girl\nCan't be bought\nAll of the boys think she's a toy\nJust because she wears nothin' but her sauce\n\nAnd if she brings her West Coast friends, they'll be like \"Oh, what a night\"\nBut we'll be smokin' in the boys' club 'til we run out of time\nSo she plays it cool, but I can see through\nShe's just a bad guy, yeah, yeah, yeah\n\nYou like that, don't you?\nDon't you, don't you, don't you?\n\nI'm a bad guy\nI'm a bad guy\nI'm a bad guy\nI'm a bad guy"}
