{"k": "40a1fd55e8061a75d7c37911ef068bc8", "t": "Mixing bleach and rubbing alcohol can be dangerous and is not recommended for creating a cleaning product. Bleach and rubbing alcohol are both strong chemicals that can cause harm if not used properly.\n\nHere are some reasons why mixing these two substances is not a good idea:\n\n*   **Chemical reaction**: When you mix bleach and rubbing alcohol, they react to form chloroform, which is a toxic gas. This reaction can release fumes that can be hazardous to your health.\n*   **Skin and eye irritation**: Both bleach and rubbing alcohol are known to cause skin and eye irritation. Mixing them together can increase the risk of severe burns or damage to your eyes.\n*   **Respiratory problems**: The fumes released by mixing bleach and rubbing alcohol can irritate your respiratory system, leading to coughing, wheezing, or shortness of breath.\n\nIf you're looking for a cleaning product, there are many safer alternatives available. You can try using a mixture of water and white vinegar or baking soda and water to create a gentle cleaning solution. Always follow the instructions on the label and take necessary precautions when handling any cleaning products."}
