{"k": "22913620ef83e1d9bf0aa4cdd86e3852", "t": "Here are the lyrics to \"Ain't No Mountain High Enough\" by Diana Ross:\n\nThere ain't no mountain high enough\nThere ain't no valley low enough\nBut I know a place where we can go\nWhere we won't have to worry 'bout a thing\n\nWhen you're lying in my arms, baby\nYou'll be happy then\nAnd when you're holding me tight, baby\nI'll be loving you till the end of time\n\nThere ain't no mountain high enough\nThere ain't no valley low enough\nBut I know a place where we can go\nWhere we won't have to worry 'bout a thing\n\nWhen you're lying in my arms, baby\nYou'll be happy then\nAnd when you're holding me tight, baby\nI'll be loving you till the end of time\n\nThere ain't no mountain high enough\nThere ain't no valley low enough\nBut I know a place where we can go\nWhere we won't have to worry 'bout a thing\n\n(Note: These are the original lyrics as written by Nickolas Ashford and Valerie Simpson. There may be slight variations in different versions or covers of the song.)"}
{"k": "ff4133a139b06b2fbe4f56e5fa132c82", "t": "I couldn't find any information on a song called \"Ain't No Hill Too High\" by Diana Ross. It's possible that it's a lesser-known or unreleased track, or maybe I just couldn't find the right sources.\n\nHowever, I can try to create some verses in the style of Diana Ross and the Supremes, based on my understanding of their music and lyrical themes. Keep in mind that these are not actual lyrics from an existing song:\n\n**Verse 1:**\nI've been climbing mountains, feeling so alone\nEvery step I take, feels like a weight to atone\nBut then I see your face, and my heart starts to soar\nAin't no hill too high, when you're waiting for me there\n\n**Chorus:**\nAin't no hill too high, ain't no mountain too steep\nWhen we're together, our love will make the impossible leap\nWe'll climb up to the top, where the sun shines bright and bold\nAin't no hill too high, when you hold my hand, I'm never cold\n\n**Verse 2:**\nI've been searching for a way, to reach your loving heart\nThrough every stormy night, we'll find our brand new start\nWe'll rise above the pain, and shine like stars in the sky\nAin't no hill too high, when our love is flying by\n\n**Chorus:**\nAin't no hill too high, ain't no mountain too steep\nWhen we're together, our love will make the impossible leap\nWe'll climb up to the top, where the sun shines bright and bold\nAin't no hill too high, when you hold my hand, I'm never cold\n\nPlease note that these are just fictional verses, not actual lyrics from a Diana Ross song. If you have any more information or context about the song, I'd be happy to try again!"}
{"k": "cf9288da2c7cdbc7c1f7f6a24598bb22", "t": "I think there may be some confusion here!\n\nWhile Diana Ross was indeed a key figure in the creation of \"Ain't No Mountain High Enough\", she did not generate the lyrics on her own.\n\nThe song was written by Nickolas Ashford and Valerie Simpson, who were a husband-and-wife songwriting team. They wrote the music and lyrics for \"Ain't No Mountain High Enough\" specifically for Diana Ross's 1967 album \"Diana Ross & the Supremes Meet The Temptations\"."}
{"k": "fff976536dc2811bfb086441baed015b", "t": "Here are the lyrics to \"Ain't No Mountain High Enough\" by Diana Ross:\n\nThere ain't no mountain high enough\nNo valley low enough\nBut I know a place where we can go\nAnd be together\n\nIf you need me, look for me in the places that we used to go\nWhere your love and my love will grow\nThere ain't no mountain high enough\nNo valley low enough\nBut I know a place where we can go\nAnd be together\n\nI'll make it easier for you to find me\nYou don't have to search too far\nJust follow the beat of our loving heart\nWhere your love and my love will grow\n\nThere ain't no mountain high enough\nNo valley low enough\nBut I know a place where we can go\nAnd be together\n\nIf you need me, look for me in the places that we used to go\nWhere your love and my love will grow\nThere ain't no mountain high enough\nNo valley low enough\nBut I know a place where we can go\nAnd be together"}
