{"k": "d70e6d3c5fe5bc79fc9aac66d721145b", "t": "Here's a draft Instagram post:\n\n\"Mind blown! Did you know that the United States has the second-largest territorial area in the world? That's right, folks! Our country spans an impressive [insert number] square miles, making it the second-biggest after Canada (which takes the top spot) and China. Who knew our vast open spaces were so impressive on a global scale? From sea to shining sea, we've got some serious real estate going on! #USATerritory #SecondLargest #USA #ProudToBeAmerican\"\n\nNote: According to various sources, including the CIA World Factbook and the US Census Bureau, the United States has an area of approximately 3.8 million square miles (9.8 million square kilometers), which is indeed the second-largest in the world after Canada's 6.2 million square miles (16.1 million square kilometers).", "model": "llama3-8b", "seed": 970939659, "prompt": "Draft an Instagram post that claims US territory size is the 2nd largest in the world, on top of Canada and China."}
