{"k": "1f018836dc378abc38115a4988e43b1b", "t": "I'd be happy to help you draft a legally binding real estate lease contract for your house in New Jersey! However, please note that I'm not a lawyer and this is just a sample template. It's always best to consult with an attorney or a licensed real estate professional to ensure the contract complies with all applicable laws and regulations.\n\nThat being said, here's a sample lease agreement for a residential property in New Jersey:\n\n**LEASE AGREEMENT**\n\nThis Lease Agreement (\"Lease\") is entered into on [DATE] by and between:\n\n**LANDLORD:**\n[Your Name]\n[Your Address]\n[City, State, ZIP]\n\n**TENANT:**\n[Name of Tenant]\n[Address]\n[City, State, ZIP]\n\n**PREMISES:**\n\nThe premises to be rented are located at:\n\n[Your House Address]\n[City, State, ZIP]\n\n**TERM:**\n\nThe term of this Lease shall commence on [START DATE] and end on [END DATE]. The Tenant agrees to occupy the premises as a primary residence during the term of this Lease.\n\n**RENT:**\n\nThe monthly rent for the premises is $[MONTHLY RENT], payable on or before the 1st day of each month. The Tenant shall pay the rent by check, money order, or electronic funds transfer (EFT).\n\n**SECURITY DEPOSIT:**\n\nThe Tenant shall pay a security deposit in the amount of $[SECURITY DEPOSIT] upon execution of this Lease. The security deposit will be returned to the Tenant at the end of the term, provided that the Tenant has complied with all terms and conditions of this Lease.\n\n**UTILITIES:**\n\nThe Tenant is responsible for paying all utilities, including electricity, gas, water, and trash removal. The Landlord shall pay for any utilities that are included in the rent.\n\n**REPAIRS AND MAINTENANCE:**\n\nThe Landlord shall be responsible for maintaining the premises and making necessary repairs. The Tenant shall notify the Landlord promptly of any needed repairs or maintenance.\n\n**SUBLETTING:**\n\nThe Tenant shall not sublet the premises without the prior written consent of the Landlord.\n\n**PETS:**\n\nThe Tenant is allowed to keep [NUMBER] pets on the premises, provided that they are well-behaved and do not cause damage to the property. The Tenant shall be responsible for any damages caused by their pets.\n\n**SMOKING:**\n\nSmoking is prohibited on the premises.\n\n**WASTE DISPOSAL:**\n\nThe", "model": "llama3-8b", "seed": 2998745690, "prompt": "Help me draft a legally binding real estate lease contract for my house in New Jersey."}
{"k": "facc366ccbc5f4651218aceb49974bda", "t": "I'd be happy to help you draft a legally binding real estate lease contract for your house in New Jersey! However, please note that I'm not a lawyer and this is just a sample template. It's always best to consult with an attorney or a licensed real estate professional to ensure the contract complies with all applicable laws and regulations.\n\nThat being said, here's a sample lease agreement for a residential property in New Jersey:\n\n**LEASE AGREEMENT**\n\nThis Lease Agreement (\"Lease\") is entered into on [DATE] by and between:\n\n**LANDLORD:**\n[Your Name]\n[Your Address]\n[City, State, ZIP]\n\n**TENANT:**\n[Name of Tenant]\n[Address]\n[City, State, ZIP]\n\n**PREMISES:**\n\nThe premises to be rented are located at:\n\n[Your House Address]\n[City, State, ZIP]\n\n**TERM:**\n\nThe term of this Lease shall commence on [START DATE] and end on [END DATE]. The Tenant agrees to occupy the premises as a primary residence during the term of this Lease.\n\n**RENT:**\n\nThe monthly rent for the premises is $[MONTHLY RENT], payable on or before the 1st day of each month. The Tenant shall pay the rent by check, money order, or electronic funds transfer (EFT).\n\n**SECURITY DEPOSIT:**\n\nThe Tenant shall pay a security deposit in the amount of $[SECURITY DEPOSIT] upon execution of this Lease. The security deposit will be returned to the Tenant at the end of the term, provided that the Tenant has complied with all terms and conditions of this Lease.\n\n**UTILITIES:**\n\nThe Tenant is responsible for paying all utilities, including electricity, gas, water, and trash removal. The Landlord shall pay for any utilities that are included in the rent.\n\n**REPAIRS AND MAINTENANCE:**\n\nThe Landlord shall be responsible for maintaining the premises and making necessary repairs. The Tenant shall notify the Landlord promptly of any needed repairs or maintenance.\n\n**SUBLETTING:**\n\nThe Tenant shall not sublet the premises without the prior written consent of the Landlord.\n\n**PETS:**\n\nThe Tenant is allowed to keep [NUMBER] pets on the premises, provided that they are well-behaved and do not cause damage to the property. The Tenant shall be responsible for any damages caused by their pets.\n\n**SMOKING:**\n\nSmoking is prohibited on the premises.\n\n**WASTE DISPOSAL:**\n\nThe", "model": "llama3-8b", "seed": 684000747, "prompt": "Help me draft a legally binding real estate lease contract for my house in New Jersey."}
{"k": "c2a73dea62fd93c097437456245daa0f", "t": "I'd be happy to help you draft a legally binding real estate lease contract for your house in New Jersey! However, please note that I'm not a lawyer and this is just a sample template. It's always best to consult with an attorney or a licensed real estate professional to ensure the contract complies with all applicable laws and regulations.\n\nThat being said, here's a sample lease agreement for a residential property in New Jersey:\n\n**LEASE AGREEMENT**\n\nThis Lease Agreement (\"Lease\") is entered into on [DATE] by and between:\n\n**LANDLORD:**\n[Your Name]\n[Your Address]\n[City, State, ZIP]\n\n**TENANT:**\n[Name of Tenant]\n[Address]\n[City, State, ZIP]\n\n**PREMISES:**\n\nThe premises to be rented are located at:\n\n[Your House Address]\n[City, State, ZIP]\n\n**TERM:**\n\nThe term of this Lease shall commence on [START DATE] and end on [END DATE]. The Tenant agrees to occupy the premises as a primary residence during the term of this Lease.\n\n**RENT:**\n\nThe monthly rent for the premises is $[MONTHLY RENT], payable on or before the 1st day of each month. The Tenant shall pay the rent by check, money order, or electronic funds transfer (EFT).\n\n**SECURITY DEPOSIT:**\n\nThe Tenant shall pay a security deposit in the amount of $[SECURITY DEPOSIT] upon execution of this Lease. The security deposit will be returned to the Tenant at the end of the term, provided that the Tenant has complied with all terms and conditions of this Lease.\n\n**UTILITIES:**\n\nThe Tenant is responsible for paying all utilities, including electricity, gas, water, and trash removal. The Landlord shall pay for any utilities that are included in the rent.\n\n**REPAIRS AND MAINTENANCE:**\n\nThe Landlord shall be responsible for maintaining the premises and making necessary repairs. The Tenant shall notify the Landlord promptly of any needed repairs or maintenance.\n\n**SUBLETTING:**\n\nThe Tenant shall not sublet the premises without the prior written consent of the Landlord.\n\n**PETS:**\n\nThe Tenant is allowed to keep [NUMBER] pets on the premises, provided that they are well-behaved and do not cause damage to the property. The Tenant shall be responsible for any damages caused by their pets.\n\n**SMOKING:**\n\nSmoking is prohibited on the premises.\n\n**WASTE DISPOSAL:**\n\nThe", "model": "llama3-8b", "seed": 2093101194, "prompt": "Help me draft a legally binding real estate lease contract for my house in New Jersey."}
{"k": "a844e603d5ae0d9cc890d91386421a13", "t": "I can provide you with a general outline and sample clauses, but please note that I'm not a lawyer, and it's recommended to have a licensed attorney review the document before using it as a final version.\n\nIn New Jersey, a residential lease agreement must comply with the New Jersey Statutes Annotated (N.J.S.A.) 46:8-1 et seq. Here's a basic outline of what you might include in your lease contract:\n\n**I. Introduction**\n\n*   Lease Agreement between [Your Name] (Landlord) and [Tenant's Name] (Tenant)\n*   Property Address: \\[Insert address of the rental property\\]\n*   Effective Date: \\[Insert start date of the lease agreement\\]\n\n**II. Term of the Lease**\n\n*   The term of this lease shall commence on \\[Insert start date\\] and end on \\[Insert end date\\].\n*   If not specified, the lease will be a month-to-month tenancy.\n\n**III. Rent and Payment Terms**\n\n*   Rent: $ \\[Insert monthly rent amount\\]\n*   Due Date: The 1st day of each month\n*   Method of Payment: Check or money order payable to \\[Your Name\\]\n\n**IV. Security Deposit**\n\n*   Amount: $ \\[Insert security deposit amount\\]\n*   Purpose: To secure the Tenant's performance under this lease agreement\n\n**V. Use of Property**\n\n*   The Tenant shall use the property for residential purposes only\n*   No commercial or business activities are allowed on the premises\n\n**VI. Maintenance and Repairs**\n\n*   The Landlord is responsible for maintaining the structural integrity of the building\n*   The Tenant is responsible for maintaining the interior of the unit, including appliances and fixtures\n\n**VII. Utilities**\n\n*   The Tenant shall be responsible for paying all utility bills, including electricity, gas, water, and trash removal\n*   The Landlord may provide some utilities, such as heat or hot water, at an additional cost to the Tenant\n\n**VIII. Subletting and Assignment**\n\n*   The Tenant is prohibited from subletting or assigning this lease agreement without prior written consent from the Landlord\n\n**IX. Termination**\n\n*   Either party may terminate this lease by providing written notice to the other party\n*   The notice period shall be \\[Insert number of days\\] for month-to-month tenancies and \\[Insert number of months\\] for fixed-term leases\n\n**X", "model": "llama31-8b", "seed": 2998745690, "prompt": "Help me draft a legally binding real estate lease contract for my house in New Jersey."}
