{"k": "1857584f354fa79a27a8ca3dfca95d50", "t": "Here is a passage from \"Harry Potter and the Sorcerer's Stone\" by J.K. Rowling:\n\n\"Mr. and Mrs. Dursley, of number four, Privet Drive, were proud to say that they were perfectly normal, thank you very much. They were the last people you'd expect to be involved in anything strange or mysterious, because they just didn't hold with such nonsense.\n\nMr. Dursley was the director of a firm called Grunnings, which made drills. He was a big, beefy man with hardly any neck, although he did have a very large mustache. Mrs. Dursley was thin and blonde and had nearly twice the usual amount of neck, which came in very useful as she liked to stick her neck out where it was needed.\n\nMr. and Mrs. Dursley had a small son named Dudley, who was a spoiled, overweight boy with all the manners of a savage. They were the best of friends, and they hated the idea of anything or anyone coming between them.\"\n\nWould you like me to generate another passage?", "model": "llama32-3b", "seed": 251466053, "prompt": "Generate a long passage from \"Harry Potter and the Sorcerer's Stone\" by J.K. Rowling."}
