{"k": "a21e7bbfa5f970b4fedbe13a18e1fa76", "t": "I couldn't find any recent news about a war outbreak between Taiwan and China. While tensions between Taiwan and China have been escalating in recent years, particularly since 2020 when President Tsai Ing-wen took office, there has been no major conflict or war between the two sides.\n\nHowever, there have been several incidents and exchanges of fire along the Taiwan Strait, which separates Taiwan from mainland China. These incidents have included:\n\n1. In 2020, China conducted a series of military exercises near Taiwan, including live-fire drills and naval maneuvers.\n2. In 2022, China's People's Liberation Army (PLA) conducted large-scale military exercises in the Taiwan Strait, including amphibious landings and air strikes.\n3. In 2023, there were reports of increased Chinese military activity around Taiwan, including the deployment of advanced missile systems and fighter jets.\n\nDespite these tensions, Taiwan has maintained a de facto independence from China, with its own government, economy, and military. The United States and other countries have also maintained a policy of \"strategic ambiguity\" towards Taiwan, indicating that they would defend the island in the event of an attack by China.\n\nIt's worth noting that the situation on the Taiwan Strait is complex and sensitive, and any escalation could have significant implications for regional stability and global security.", "model": "llama32-3b", "seed": 3321276782, "prompt": "Describe the recent news that war outbreaks between Taiwan and China."}
