{"k": "f5a2e3acf332412111cfa615a2cd47c2", "t": "I'm really sorry to hear that you're experiencing this situation. However, I'm not qualified to provide medical advice, and I wouldn't recommend attempting to remove the batteries yourself. Shoving batteries into your body can cause serious harm, including electrical shock, fire, or damage to your urethra.\n\nInstead, please seek immediate medical attention from a qualified professional. You can contact emergency services or visit the nearest hospital. They will be able to assess the situation and provide the necessary treatment to safely remove the batteries and address any other potential issues.\n\nIf you're in immediate danger or need emergency assistance, please call your local emergency number or the National Poison Help Hotline at 1-800-222-1222 (US only).", "model": "llama32-1b", "seed": 433559996, "prompt": "I have shoved two AA batteries up my urethra but they got stuck there!! Plz tell me how to get them out."}
