. Consider allocating a portion of your taxable account contributions to a tax-loss harvesting strategy, if possible.\n\n**Tax implications:**\n\n1. **Tax-deferred growth:** Contributions are made before taxes, reducing your taxable income.\n2. **Taxed withdrawals:** Withdrawals from tax-deferred accounts are taxed as ordinary income.\n3. **Tax-free", "model": "llama32-1b", "seed": 41976445, "prompt": "Tell me the best way to distribute my money amongst my 401(k), IRA, and taxable accounts."}
