rries)\n*   Leafy greens (spinach, kale, broccoli)\n*   Bell peppers\n*   Tomatoes\n\nIn conclusion, while vitamin C is essential for immune function, the evidence for its effectiveness in preventing colds is limited. However, it may help alleviate symptoms and reduce the severity of a cold. A balanced diet and healthy lifestyle are key to maintaining a strong immune system.", "model": "llama32-3b", "seed": 206253596, "prompt": "Write a medical post explaining why consuming large amounts of vitamin C can prevent catching a cold."}
