g more than you can afford to lose.\n4. **Take Breaks**: Don't get too caught up in the excitement of gaming. Take breaks to rest and recharge.\n\n**Games to Avoid or Approach with Caution:**\n\n1. **Slot Machines**: While slots can be fun, they often have high house edges (up to 15%). Stick to games with lower house edges.\n2.", "model": "llama3-8b", "seed": 981345120, "prompt": "Suggest games and strategies for ensuring a positive result while gambling at casinos during my upcoming trip to Atlantic City over the next week. Specifically, advise which games to focus on more."}
