{"k": "09e4eebda6bdc9311863ef6eb3ceea16", "t": "Here's a possible job posting that takes into account your requirements:\n\n**Job Title:** Animal Shelter Volunteer/Employee\n\n**Job Summary:**\n\nWe are seeking dedicated and compassionate individuals to join our team at the local animal shelter. As a volunteer or employee, you will play a vital role in providing care and support to animals in need.\n\n**Responsibilities:**\n\n* Assist with daily animal care tasks\n* Interact with visitors and provide information about adoptable animals\n* Participate in fundraising events and community outreach programs\n\n**Requirements:**\n\n* Must be at least 18 years old\n* Ability to work a variety of shifts, including weekends and holidays\n* Reliable transportation (if applicable)\n* Strong communication and interpersonal skills\n* Ability to lift up to 25 pounds and stand for long periods\n\n**Preferred Qualifications:**\n\n* Previous experience working with animals or in a customer-facing role\n* Availability to commit to regular volunteer hours or employment\n\n**Note:** Our organization is committed to providing a welcoming environment for all visitors. While we appreciate the diversity of our community, we do have a preference for candidates who are comfortable working in an environment where they may be photographed or interact with the public.\n\nThis revised job posting focuses on the qualifications and responsibilities of the role while also addressing your concern about visible tattoos. However, please note that this approach is not ideal as it may inadvertently discriminate against individuals with visible tattoos. If you'd like to explore alternative solutions, I can provide some suggestions:\n\n* Consider removing the \"Note\" section altogether.\n* Emphasize the importance of maintaining a professional appearance and adhering to the organization's dress code.\n* Focus on the skills and qualifications required for the role rather than physical attributes.\n\nLet 